{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghrYc1z7ffL58PBRtVBt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01H3i2sTfb6S36toz1bvK5kA","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-050308__x1f94fb/work/PLAN.md","offset":300,"limit":330},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11189,"cache_read_input_tokens":24726,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11189},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66d97bf5-dd15-40b7-85f8-8eecadfc963f","uuid":"6dd845e6-01f8-40bf-873a-c39dd81499cf","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:03:27.165Z","request_id":"req_011CghrYbnbRk7H6YFiMp74s","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01H3i2sTfb6S36toz1bvK5kA":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-050308__x1f94fb/work/PLAN.md","offset":300,"limit":330}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01H3i2sTfb6S36toz1bvK5kA","type":"tool_result","content":"300\t\n301\t### 3.1 The core loop (must feel instant)\n302\t\n303\tTrack select → **flyover** (2.5 s camera sweep along the route with the track name; any button skips) → **3-2-1-GO**\n304\t(start-gate lights, Monsieur Drapeau drops the flag, beeps, gibberish count) → drive → each checkpoint shows the split\n305\tand the delta to your best (blue `-0.42` ahead, red `+0.31` behind) → **FINISH** (slow-mo 0.6 s, camera swings\n306\tround) → results (time, delta, medal drop-in, coppers count-up) → **Retry is one button and takes under half a\n307\tsecond.** In play: **Respawn** puts you at the last checkpoint, standing, the clock still running (TrackMania 2003's\n308\tclassic respawn); **Restart** goes back to the start with a short 1-second \"READY... GO\". Both work at any moment,\n309\tincluding mid-air. The ghost of your best run (translucent) races with you; Coco's ghost (the author time, generated\n310\tby the bot) can be switched on in Settings.\n311\t\n312\t### 3.2 Input maps (`game.input` presets; prompts always from `game.input.label(action)` + our glyph sprites)\n313\t\n314\tRace (`RACE_INPUT`; analog via E4 `input.analog`):\n315\t\n316\t| Action | DualSense (standard mapping) | Keyboard | Notes |\n317\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n318\t| steer | left stick X (analog), d-pad ←/→ | ←/→, A/D | `input.move()[0]`; keyboard steering ramps (see §4.4 `steerRamp`) |\n319\t| gas | R2 (Pad7, analog), ✕ (Pad0) | ↑, W | analog value 0..1 |\n320\t| brake / reverse | L2 (Pad6, analog), □ (Pad2) | ↓, S | brake + steer at speed = drift (§4.4) |\n321\t| respawn (last CP) | ○ (Pad1) | Enter, Backspace | TrackMania habit |\n322\t| restart (from start) | △ (Pad3) | Delete, R | |\n323\t| camera (far → close → hood) | R1 (Pad5) | C (also 1/2/3 pick one) | |\n324\t| ghost on/off | L1 (Pad4) | G | |\n325\t| horn (just for fun: two-tone toot + gibberish \"beep beep\") | R3 (Pad11) | H | |\n326\t| pause | Options (Pad9) | Esc, P | engine standard |\n327\t\n328\tMouse in races: none (racing doesn't aim); the cursor hides while driving and reappears on menus.\n329\t\n330\tMenus (engine `up/down/left/right/confirm/cancel` + ours): d-pad/left stick move focus; ✕/Enter/Space choose;\n331\t○/Esc/Backspace back; L1/R1 or Q/E switch tabs; △/Y \"secondary\" (e.g. ghost toggle on track select, reset on a\n332\tslider); **mouse hover moves the focus, click chooses, wheel scrolls lists**. Repeat on hold (`input.repeat`).\n333\t\n334\tEditor (`EDIT_INPUT`, §5.4) and replay (`REPLAY_INPUT`, §5.8) have their own tables in their sections.\n335\t\n336\tRumble (`input.rumble`): wall hits (∝ impact), hard landings, boost pads (short), checkpoint (tiny), finish.\n337\t\n338\t**AI Hub reserved:** in a session, ignore Options (pause) while Create (Pad8) is held.\n339\t\n340\t### 3.3 10-foot UI rules (apply everywhere)\n341\t\n342\t- Buffer is `res: 'ps1', expand: true` (~427×240 on 16:9). Primary text: pixel font at **scale 2** (14 px of 240 ≈\n343\t  6% of screen height). Secondary text scale 1, never the `tiny` font for anything the player must read. Big numbers\n344\t  (timer, speed) use a custom chunky digit sprite at 2–3× (§7.6).\n345\t- Tiles at least 96×64 buffer px, 8 px gaps, 12 px safe margins (and keep clear of the engine's top-right corner\n346\t  buttons: `game.cornerArea()`).\n347\t- One focused element always visible (accent border + 1.08× scale tween + a soft glow); spatial navigation; hover =\n348\t  focus; click = choose. Every screen has a back path (○/Esc/right-click).\n349\t- A **prompt bar** along the bottom of every screen: `[glyph] Select  [glyph] Back  [glyph] ...` — glyphs follow\n350\t  `input.lastDevice` (PlayStation shapes by default; Xbox letters if the Settings \"Button symbols\" is Xbox; keycaps\n351\t  for keyboard; mouse icons when the mouse was last used).\n352\t- No dense data screens: at most 6 numbers on any results/records panel; lists show 5–7 rows at scale 2 with\n353\t  scrolling.\n354\t- Colour is never the only signal (deltas carry `+`/`−`, medals carry letters B/S/G/A on their icons).\n355\t\n356\t---\n357\t\n358\t## 4. Core systems\n359\t\n360\t### 4.1 Blocks (the catalogue)\n361\t\n362\tEvery track — campaign, puzzle, editor — is a list of placements `{ type, cx, cy, L, rot }` (rot = heading of the\n363\tblock's local +x: 0 E, 1 S, 2 W, 3 N). In its **local frame** a block's entry is the centre of the west face of local\n364\tcell (0,0) at level 0, heading +x; local y is to the right (south when rot = 0). Footprint offsets below are\n365\t`(along, right, levels)`.\n366\t\n367\t| Type | Token | Footprint (along × right × levels) | Exit (local cell, heading) | Geometry | Surface | Cost (¢) | Envs |\n368\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n369\t| Start | `ST` | 1×1×1 | (1,0) → +x | straight; spawn at s = 8 m; start arch at s = 10 m | road | 0 (max 1) | all |\n370\t| Finish | `FN` | 1×1×1 | (1,0) → +x | straight; finish arch at s = 16 m | road | 0 (≥1) | all |\n371\t| Checkpoint | `CP` | 1×1×1 | (1,0) | straight; gate at s = 16 m | road | 15 | all |\n372\t| Straight | `S` | 1×1×1 | (1,0) | straight | road | 5 | all |\n373\t| Boost | `BO` | 1×1×1 | (1,0) | straight + boost pad (s 10–22 m) | road+boost | 40 | all |\n374\t| Turn, tight | `L1`/`R1` | 1×1×1 | side cell | quarter circle r = 16 m | road | 8 | all |\n375\t| Turn, wide | `L2`/`R2` | 2×2×1 | (1, ±2) heading ±y | quarter circle r = 48 m | road | 15 | all |\n376\t| Turn, sweeping | `L3`/`R3` | 3×3×1 | (2, ±3) heading ±y | quarter circle r = 80 m | road | 25 | all |\n377\t| Banked turn | `BL2`/`BR2` | 2×2×2 | as L2/R2 | r = 48 m, bank 0→28°→0 (sin ramp) | road | 30 | Dustbowl, Frostpeak |\n378\t| Hill up/down (steep) | `U1`/`D1` | 1×1×2 | (1,0), level ±1 | smoothstep rise 8 m over 32 m (max grade 37.5%: launches you at speed) | road | 10 | all |\n379\t| Hill up/down | `U2`/`D2` | 2×1×2 | (2,0), level ±1 | smoothstep rise 8 m over 64 m (max 18.75%) | road | 15 | all |\n380\t| Kicker | `KI` | 1×1×2 | none (air) | concave arc to a **15° lip, 4.2 m high** at s = 32 m (arc radius 123.6 m) | road | 30 | all |\n381\t| Landing | `LA` | 2×1×2 | (2,0) | air entry; smoothstep descent from +3 m to 0 over 64 m | road | 20 | all |\n382\t| Gap | `GAPn` | n×1×2 reserved air | — | nothing (a reserved corridor); the track's **chasm** list (default: its level-0 GAP cells) cuts the base plate | — | 0 | all |\n383\t| Loop | `LOOPR`/`LOOPL` | 2×2×4 | (2, ±1) → +x | §4.2: 12 m-radius loop with a one-cell sideways shift; lane assist | road | 120 | all |\n384\t| Crossing | `CR` | 1×1×1 | all four faces | flat square deck, 4 ports | road | 20 | all |\n385\t| Bumps | `BU` | 1×1×1 | (1,0) | three 0.5 m humps (`z = 0.5·sin²(3πs/32)`) | road | 10 | Hedgerow |\n386\t| Dirt straight / turns | `DS`, `DL1`/`DR1`, `DL2`/`DR2` | as S / L1 / L2 | | | dirt | as base | Hedgerow, Dustbowl |\n387\t| Ice straight / turns | `IS`, `IL1`/`IR1`, `IL2`/`IR2` | as S / L1 / L2 | | | ice | as base | Frostpeak |\n388\t| Deco items | (editor only) | 1×1 | — | scenery props from §7.4 | — | 5–25 | per env |\n389\t\n390\tTurtle rules (§6.1) for where the next block goes follow from the \"Exit\" column: a turn of size n fills the n×n square\n391\t`c0 + a·h + b·s` (a, b ∈ [0, n)) and exits into `c0 + (n−1)·h + n·s` heading `s` (s = the turn side); a loop fills a\n392\t2×2×4 box and exits into `c0 + 2h + s` with the heading unchanged; hills occupy their cells on both levels they span;\n393\ta kicker reserves the level above its cell; `GAPn` reserves n cells on levels L and L+1.\n394\t\n395\t**Ports and links.** A port = (world cell, face, level, heading). Two blocks connect when a port of one and a port of\n396\tthe other share the face, level, and opposite headings. Straight-like blocks are symmetric (drivable both ways); turns,\n397\thills, kickers, landings, loops, start and finish are directional for the route (a car can still drive them\n398\tbackwards physically). **Jump links:** a kicker links to the first landing (or any block whose entry faces it) found\n399\talong its heading within 5 cells, on the kicker's level or up to 3 levels lower. The **route** is the chain of links\n400\tfrom Start to Finish (§4.8); the editor shows unlinked ports as red arrows.\n401\t\n402\t### 4.2 Block paths (centrelines and frames)\n403\t\n404\tEach block type exports `path(s) -> { p, t, u }` for s ∈ [0, len] in local metres (p position, t unit tangent, u unit\n405\tup), plus `width(s)`, `bank`, and `surface(s)`. Right is `r = u × t`. Formulas (local frame, entry at (0,0,0), +x\n406\tforward, +y right):\n407\t\n408\t- **Straight** (n cells): `p = (s, 0, 0)`, `t = (1,0,0)`, `u = (0,0,1)`, `len = 32n`.\n409\t- **Turn R, radius ρ = 32n − 16** (n = 1, 2, 3): `φ = s/ρ`, `p = (ρ sin φ, ρ(1 − cos φ), 0)`, `t = (cos φ, sin φ, 0)`,\n410\t  `len = πρ/2`. L mirrors y. Check: n = 1 exits at (16, 16) — the centre of the south face of cell (0,0).\n411\t- **Banked**: as the turn; bank `β(φ) = 28°·sin(2φ)` (0 at both ports, 28° mid-bend); `u = cos β·ẑ + sin β·r̂_in` where `r̂_in` points to the\n412\t  turn centre (right for R). The road edge on the outside rises; the ports stay flat.\n413\t- **Hill Un** (rise H = 8 m over len = 32n): `z(s) = H·(3x² − 2x³)`, x = s/len; `t ∝ (1, 0, z'(s))`;\n414\t  `u ∝ (−z'(s), 0, 1)`. D mirrors (descends). The U1 crest has radius ≈ 21 m: above ~60 km/h the car takes off (by\n415\t  design); U2's crest (≈ 85 m) holds the car up to ~150 km/h.\n416\t- **Kicker**: `z(s) = ρk − sqrt(ρk² − s²)`, ρk = 123.6 m, s ∈ [0, 32]: lip angle 15°, lip height 4.2 m.\n417\t- **Landing**: `z(s) = 3·(1 − (3x² − 2x³))`, x = s/64.\n418\t- **Loop R** (exit one cell right, two cells ahead, same heading). Let `S = 32 + 2π·12 + 32` (≈ 139.4 m) be the\n419\t  total centreline length and `y(s) = 32·(3q² − 2q³)` with q = s/S (the sideways shift spread over the whole piece).\n420\t  For s ∈ [0, 32]: `p = (s, y, 0)`; for the circle (θ = (s − 32)/12 ∈ [0, 2π]): `p = (32 + 12 sin θ, y, 12(1 − cos θ))`,\n421\t  `u0 = (−sin θ, 0, cos θ)`; for s ∈ [32 + 24π, S]: `p = (32 + (s − 32 − 24π), y, 0)` — i.e. the circle's bottom is at\n422\t  local x = 32, entering and leaving there, shifted sideways. Tangent = normalized derivative (numerical, h = 0.01 m);\n423\t  up = `u0` Gram–Schmidt'ed against t. At the circle's bottom points the entry and exit lanes are ~23 m apart, more\n424\t  than a road width, so the ribbons never touch. L mirrors y. The loop block has **lane assist** (§4.4 step 7).\n425\t- **Crossing**: a flat 32×32 m deck; its \"path\" for routing is the straight line through the two opposite ports the\n426\t  route uses.\n427\t\n428\tPort frames must match exactly between linked blocks (position within 1 cm, tangent and up within 0.5°): a test checks\n429\tevery link of every shipped track (§9).\n430\t\n431\t### 4.3 Geometry, materials and colliders\n432\t\n433\t**Ribbon mesher.** Sample each block path every 1 m (curves) or per cell (straights; 4 segments), and at each sample\n434\tlay the environment's **cross-section** (a list of (lateral offset, height, uv.u, part) points) along `r` and `u`.\n435\tParts: `road`, `line` (baked into the road texture), `curb`, `rail` (vertical barrier), `bank` (snowbank / hedge /\n436\tstone wall), `underside`. Output per part: render triangles (three winding) + UVs (u across in metres/2, v along in\n437\tmetres/4 so the pixel textures tile at ~8–12 cm per texel) and collision triangles (Rapier winding, engine units) with a\n438\tsurface tag.\n439\t\n440\t| Env | Road width | Curb | Elevated edge | Ground-level edge | Supports under elevated pieces |\n441\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n442\t| Dustbowl | 14 m asphalt, yellow centre dashes, white edges | 1 m red/white, +0.2 m, drivable | steel guard rail 0.9 m (solid) | sand (base plate) | concrete pillars 1.4 m square every 16 m along both edges |\n443\t| Hedgerow | 12 m tarmac (or dirt), white edges | 0.8 m white/green | low stone wall 0.8 m (solid) | grass verge; hedges on some pieces (deco) | earth embankment (45° grassy slopes, drivable, slow) |\n444\t| Frostpeak | 12 m packed-snow road (or ice), orange edge poles every 8 m (deco) | 0.8 m blue/white | snowbank 1.2 m (sloped, low grip: pushes you back) | snow | rock-and-snow embankment |\n445\t\n446\t- Turns and banked turns get the elevated-edge barrier on their **outer** edge even at ground level (Dustbowl: tyre\n447\t  wall instead of rail).\n448\t- Loops get 0.5 m lips both sides. Kickers and landings get curbs only. Gaps get nothing.\n449\t- **Base plate** (per track): one mesh of the grid's cells minus the track's chasm cells (§6.3); environment ground\n450\t  texture (sand ripples / mown grass stripes / snow with sparkles). Collider: one trimesh, surface = the env's\n451\t  off-road surface. **Chasm walls**: for each chasm cell edge that borders plate, a vertical quad down 60 m with the\n452\t  terrain rock texture (canyons) or down 2 m to a water surface mesh (streams, ponds; water is a `water` trigger). **Boundary**: a 2 m wall all round the grid (Dustbowl: striped concrete barriers; Hedgerow: dry\n453\t  stone wall; Frostpeak: snow fence) with a collider.\n454\t- **Materials** (made once per world at boot): `MeshLambertNodeMaterial({ map })` for road/curb/ground/supports with\n455\t  the baked textures (`NearestFilter`, repeat, sRGB) — this matches the engine's level look; walls/rails/props in\n456\t  `MeshToonNodeMaterial({ map, gradientMap: World3D.TOON_BANDS })` (E6). Track meshes are environment (not added to\n457\t  `world._obj`), so the \"objects\" filter mode leaves them alone. Cast/receive shadows on all track meshes.\n458\t- **Gates, boards, boost chevrons, edge poles, flags** are drawn with `world.pen` every frame (animated; a few dozen\n459\t  parts each). Gate posts also get box colliders.\n460\t- **Colliders** live in `TrackPhysics`'s own `RAPIER.World` (gravity irrelevant, never stepped with bodies; call\n461\t  `pw.step()` once after adding/removing colliders so queries see them). One trimesh collider per block (road + curbs\n462\t  + lips + underside) tagged with its surface(s) — if a block mixes surfaces (boost pad), split it into one collider\n463\t  per surface. Barriers/walls as separate trimesh colliders tagged `wall`. `Map(collider.handle → { blockId, surface })`.\n464\t- Rapier 0.19.3 JS facts verified while planning: `castRayAndGetNormal(ray, maxToi, solid, flags, groups,\n465\t  excludeCollider, excludeBody)` → `{ timeOfImpact, normal, collider, featureType, featureId }` (camelCase);\n466\t  `castShape(pos, rot, vel, shape, targetDistance, maxToi, stopAtPenetration, ...)` → `{ time_of_impact, witness1,\n467\t  witness2, normal1, normal2, collider }` (snake_case `time_of_impact`); `projectPoint(p, solid)` → `{ point,\n468\t  isInside, collider, ... }`; `intersectionsWithShape(pos, rot, shape, cb)`. Take a wall normal as `normal2` flipped,\n469\t  if needed, so it opposes the motion.\n470\t\n471\t### 4.4 The car (validated model — build exactly this, then tune with Dev Mode)\n472\t\n473\tThe car is **not** a physics body. Each step (1/120 s) it probes the track with four wheel rays, follows the surface\n474\tit's on with velocity-level constraints, and flies ballistically when the surface can't hold it. This is what makes\n475\tloops hold when you're fast and drop you when you're slow — TrackMania's feel — and it's deterministic.\n476\t\n477\tState (engine units): `p` (chassis reference point: centre of the wheelbase, `ride` above the road), `v`, frame\n478\t`f, u` (r derived), `grounded`, `n` (surface normal last step), `kappa` (filtered curvature), `load` (normal load per\n479\tunit mass), `slip` (detach timer),\n480\t`air` (seconds airborne), `flop` (crash-recovery timer), `boostT`, `drift`, `surface`, `blockId`, per-wheel `d` (for\n481\tdrawing suspension), `steerVis`, `slide` (for FX/sound), `impact` (last impact speed).\n482\t\n483\t```text\n484\tstep(car, ctl{steer -1..1, gas 0..1, brake 0..1}, dt):\n485\t  g = (0, 0, -G)                                   G = CFG.gravity (default 1.5 g = 14.7 m/s²)\n486\t  1 PROBE: for each wheel mount m_i = p + f·lx_i + r·ly_i (lx = ±wheelbase/2, ly = ±track/2):\n487\t       origin = m_i + u·0.5 m; ray along −u, length 0.5 m + ride + reach (reach = 0.9 m)\n488\t       hit -> point_i, normal_i, d_i = toi − 0.5 m, surface_i (collider map)\n489\t  2 SURFACE: if 4 hits: n = normalize(cross(FR − RL, FL − RR)), flipped to agree with u   (plane through the\n490\t       contacts: smooth on a faceted mesh — averaging triangle normals made the car let go at the top of the loop)\n491\t     else if ≥ 2 hits: n = normalize(Σ normal_i); else no surface.  d̄ = mean d_i.\n492\t  3 CONTACT:\n493\t     if n:\n494\t       vn = v·n;  pull = g·n  (> 0: gravity pulls the car off this surface)\n495\t       if grounded: k0 = −((n − car.n)·v̂) / max(1, |v|·dt);  car.kappa += (k0 − car.kappa)·min(1, dt/0.04)\n496\t       else car.kappa = 0\n497\t       vt2 = |v|² − vn²;  Aeff = A·min(1, sqrt(vt2) / 15 m/s)   A = CFG.adhesion (0.35 g), fading out at low speed\n498\t       load = vt2·car.kappa − pull + Aeff                         (normal load per unit mass; ≥ 0: the surface holds you)\n499\t       car.slip = load >= 0 ? 0 : car.slip + dt\n500\t       stay = grounded ? (car.slip < 0.06 s && d̄ < ride + reach)\n501\t                       : (vn < 0 && d̄ < ride + 0.6·reach)        (landing)\n502\t     grounded = n && stay\n503\t  4 GROUNDED:\n504\t     if just landed: impact = −vn; if u·n < 0.3 -> FLOP (step 8); else v −= n·vn,\n505\t                     v *= 1 − clamp((impact − 6 m/s)·0.02, 0, 0.25); landing FX (dust ring, thump, shake ∝ impact)\n506\t     u = normalize(u + (n − u)·min(1, 30·dt));  f = normalize(f − u(f·u));  r = u × f\n507\t     v −= n(v·n)                                                  (no motion into or off the surface)\n508\t     s = v·f\n509\t     a = g − n(g·n)                                               (gravity along the surface: slopes matter)\n510\t     traction = surface.grip·max(0, load)                         (what the tyres can pass on: μ·N/m)\n511\t     gas:   if s < vtop: a += f·min(traction, gas·A0·(1 − (max(s,0)/vtop)^1.6))\n512\t     brake: if s > 0.5 m/s: a −= v̂·min(traction, brake·B) (clamp so v doesn't reverse this step)\n513\t            else: a −= f·min(traction, brake·Arev) while s > −vrev   (reverse)\n514\t     coast: if gas = 0: a −= v̂·1.2 m/s²;  rolling: a −= v̂·surface.roll;  aero: a −= v·cd·|v|\n515\t     boost: if boostT > 0: a += f·CFG.boostAccel; boostT −= dt\n516\t     steering (bicycle model): δmax = lerp(δlo, δhi, clamp(|s|/vtop, 0, 1)^0.7)\n517\t       steerIn: keyboard input ramps to ±1 over 0.12 s and back over 0.08 s; sticks apply directly (deadzone by engine)\n518\t       drift = brake > 0.5 && |steer| > 0.5 && s > 60 km/h (TrackMania's brake-drift)\n519\t       yawRate = s·tan(steer·δmax)/wheelbase·(drift ? 1.3 : 1)\n520\t       f = rotate(f, about u, yawRate·dt); r = u × f\n521\t     grip: vlat = v·r; maxDv = grip·surface.grip·(load/G)·(drift ? driftGrip : 1)·dt   (= the tuned grip on flat\n522\t           ground; more when pressed into a loop or bank, less over a crest or upside down)\n523\t           dv = clamp(−vlat, −maxDv, maxDv); v += r·dv; slide = |vlat| − |dv|\n524\t     v += a·dt;  p += v·dt;  p += n·(ride − d̄)·min(1, 25·dt)        (ride-height spring on position)\n525\t     car.n = n;  surface = most common surface_i;  boost pad: entering a boost collider while grounded ->\n526\t       v += f·CFG.boostDv (cap at 1.3·vtop), boostT = CFG.boostTime (re-arm after leaving that pad)\n527\t  5 AIRBORNE:\n528\t     v += g·dt;  v −= v·cdAir·|v|·dt;  p += v·dt;  air += dt\n529\t     f = rotate(f, about u, ctl.steer·airYaw·dt)                  (air steering)\n530\t     f = normalize(f + (v̂ − f)·min(1, 1.5·dt)); r = normalize(u × f); u = normalize(f × r)   (nose follows the arc)\n531\t     u = normalize(u + (ẑ − u)·min(1, 0.8·dt)), re-orthonormalize   (gentle roll levelling: no side landings after a\n532\t                                                                       mistimed loop)\n533\t  6 WALLS (both states, after moving): cast the chassis box (half extents L/2, W/2, 0.45 m; centre p + u·0.35 m;\n534\t     rotation from (f, r, u)) from the old to the new position with castShape (targetDistance 0.02 m). Ignore hits\n535\t     whose normal nw has |nw·u| > 0.65 (that's ground, step 3 owns it). On a wall hit: move to the contact\n536\t     (time_of_impact), vN = v·nw; v −= nw·vN·(1 + e) (e = 0.15); v *= 1 − 0.1·min(1, |vN|/10);\n537\t     turn f toward the wall tangent by up to 0.25 rad; slide the remaining motion once more; sparks at witness1;\n538\t     scrape sound while touching; |vN| > 15 m/s = crash (shake, rumble, big sparks). If the box starts overlapping\n539\t     a wall (intersectionsWithShape), restore the previous p and remove the inward velocity.\n540\t  7 LANE ASSIST (only on blocks with assist: loops): find the nearest centreline sample of the current block, lateral\n541\t     error e (along r) and its rate; f = rotate(f, about u, clamp(−0.35·e/1m − 0.08·ė/(1 m/s), −1, 1)·1.2·dt).\n542\t     CFG.loopAssist (on by default; a Setting and a Dev slider) scales it.\n543\t  8 FLOP: when landing on the side/roof (u·n < 0.3) or stuck upside down: 0.6 s animation that rotates the car\n544\t     upright onto the surface below, v *= 0.3, inputs ignored. Cartoonish, keeps flow; respawn is still one button.\n545\t  9 OUT OF BOUNDS: p.z < −25 m (fell into a chasm or off the world) -> auto-respawn after a 0.4 s fade.\n546\t```\n547\t\n548\tPrototype results (headless, Rapier 0.19.3 trimesh ribbons, Appendix A's code exactly as printed: Coyote tuning,\n549\tG = 1.5 g, adhesion 0.35 g, ride 0.55 m, reach 0.9 m): **12 m loop on full throttle** — 40 km/h entry drops off the\n550\ttop, 47 km/h holds (46 km/h over the top), 59–102 km/h hold; **coasting** — 101 km/h drops off, 107 km/h holds;\n551\t**15° kicker, 64 m gap, landing pad from +3 m** — 135 km/h at the lip falls into the gap, 161 / 181 / 194 km/h land\n552\tupright 9 / 29 / 45 m into the pad after 1.65–2.07 s of air. Two lessons from the spike: averaging triangle normals\n553\tinstead of the four-point plane made the car let go on every flat facet of the loop (keep the plane fit); without\n554\ttraction limits the engine pushed the car up the loop from any speed (keep `traction`). In a full-course run with a\n555\tsideways-shifted loop (as the loop block has), the car stayed on only with lane assist — keep it on loop blocks.\n556\t\n557\t**Car tuning (defaults; all live in Dev Mode):**\n558\t\n559\t| | Coyote (Dustbowl) | Pebble (Hedgerow) | Moose (Frostpeak) |\n560\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n561\t| Body L×W×H (m) | 4.4 × 1.9 × 1.25 | 3.8 × 1.75 × 1.35 | 4.1 × 1.95 × 1.7 |\n562\t| Wheelbase / track / wheel radius (m) | 2.7 / 1.6 / 0.36 | 2.4 / 1.5 / 0.32 | 2.5 / 1.65 / 0.45 |\n563\t| ride (m) | 0.55 | 0.50 | 0.70 |\n564\t| vtop | 230 km/h | 195 km/h | 175 km/h |\n565\t| A0 (accel at 0) / B (brake) / Arev, vrev | 12 / 24 m/s² / 6, 40 km/h | 14 / 28 / 6, 40 | 11 / 22 / 6, 40 |\n566\t| δlo / δhi (steer at 0 / top speed) | 34° / 7° | 36° / 9° | 32° / 9° |\n567\t| grip (lateral, asphalt) | 15 m/s² | 18 m/s² | 14 m/s² |\n568\t| driftGrip | 0.55 | 0.70 | 0.60 |\n569\t| airYaw | 1.2 rad/s | 1.5 rad/s | 1.0 rad/s |\n570\t| cd / cdAir | 0.0004 /m | 0.0004 | 0.0005 |\n571\t| adhesion | 0.35 g | 0.35 g | 0.40 g |\n572\t\n573\tGlobal: gravity 1.5 g; boostDv 10 m/s; boostAccel 7 m/s²; boostTime 1.2 s; wall e 0.15.\n574\t\n575\t**Surfaces** (`grip` multiplier per car, `roll` = rolling resistance m/s²):\n576\t\n577\t| Surface | Coyote | Pebble | Moose | roll | FX / sound |\n578\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n579\t| road (asphalt / tarmac / packed snow road) | 1.0 | 1.0 | 1.0 | 0.15 | tyre squeal |\n580\t| dirt | 0.75 | 0.95 | 0.85 | 0.6 | brown dust, crunch |\n581\t| grass (verge, embankment) | 0.55 | 0.60 | 0.65 | 2.5 | green bits |\n582\t| sand (Dustbowl plate) | 0.50 | 0.55 | 0.60 | 4.0 | sand plume |\n583\t| snow (Frostpeak plate, snowbank) | 0.60 | 0.65 | 0.90 | 1.2 | snow spray |\n584\t| ice | 0.30 | 0.35 | 0.55 | 0.05 | ice hiss, sparkles |\n585\t| boost | as road | | | 0.15 | chevrons flash |\n586\t\n587\t### 4.5 Cameras (`car/camera.js`; all through `world.camera` in `'fixed'` mode with `up`, E2)\n588\t\n589\tSet `world.camera.mouseLook = false` (no pointer lock in races). Compute in steps, place in `onDraw` interpolated with\n590\t`game.alpha` (the engine leaves a pose set in `onDraw` to the game).\n591\t- **Far chase (default):** target `T = p + u·1.2 m + f·3 m`; smoothed frame `fc` (forward) and `uc` (up) chase the\n592\t  car's `f, u` at 6/s and 4/s while grounded; in the air `fc` follows `v̂` and `uc` eases to ẑ at 1.5/s (the camera\n593\t  doesn't spin with flips). Position `T − fc·(6.5 m + 0.012 s·|v|) + uc·2.0 m`. FOV 70° + 12°·clamp((kmh − 100)/150,\n594\t  0, 1) + 6° while boosting (reduce-motion: no FOV kick). If a ray from T to the camera hits the track, pull in.\n595\t- **Close chase:** 4.2 m back, 1.3 m up, FOV 75°. **Hood:** `p + f·0.6 + u·1.15`, look along f, up u, FOV 80°; the\n596\t  pen draws the bonnet and a dashboard strip (the overlay pen, as the shooter kit draws a gun) so it reads as a car.\n597\t- **Flyover (intro):** samples the route; the camera rides 25 m above and 30 m beside the route from start to finish\n598\t  over 2.5 s (smoothstep), then cuts behind the car.\n599\t- **Finish orbit:** 10 m radius around the car, 0.35 rad/s, slight slow-motion (`game.timeScale = .35` for 0.6 s).\n600\t- **TV (replays):** trackside spots generated along the route every ~5 blocks, 25 m to the side and 6 m up; the\n601\t  nearest spot with a clear line of sight films; FOV narrows to keep the car ~1/4 of screen height.\n602\t- **Orbit/free (replays, results):** right stick / mouse drag orbit, triggers / wheel zoom.\n603\t- **Editor:** orbit around the cursor (yaw, pitch 25°–80°, distance 60–400 m), smoothed (§5.4).\n604\t- Split screen: one `world.addCamera()` per extra viewport, each with its own chase state.\n605\t\n606\t### 4.6 A run (`race/run.js`)\n607\t\n608\t- Phases: `intro` (flyover) → `countdown` (3 s; 1 s on restart) → `racing` → `finished` | `abandoned`.\n609\t- The clock counts **steps** from GO; the car is held (brakes on, gas revs the engine sound only) before GO.\n610\t- **Gates:** each CP/finish gate is a plane (point, normal = path tangent, half-width = road half-width + 1 m,\n611\t  height 7 m above the road along u). A crossing = the segment from the previous to the new car position crosses\n612\t  the plane within those bounds. **Checkpoints count once each, in any order, either direction** (TrackMania).\n613\t  **Finish counts only forward and only with every checkpoint passed**; otherwise show \"MISSING CHECKPOINT\" once.\n614\t- **Respawn:** to the last checkpoint passed (or the start): car at the gate (or spawn) frame, `v = 0`, upright,\n615\t  `boostT = 0`; the clock keeps running; respawn counter +1; warp-in FX (glints, a quick scale-in, rising arpeggio).\n616\t- **Restart:** new run object; ghost recording restarts; respawn counter 0.\n617\t- **Splits:** per run, the step count at each CP in the order passed; compare to the best run's splits (by order).\n618\t- Events emitted for HUD/sound/FX: `cp(i, steps, delta)`, `finish(steps, delta, medal)`, `respawn`, `restart`,\n619\t  `boost`, `land(impact)`, `wall(impact)`, `flop`, `missingCp`.\n620\t\n621\t### 4.7 Ghosts and replays (`race/ghost.js`)\n622\t\n623\t- Record every 4th step (30 Hz): position (int16 deltas in 1/16 unit — 1/256 m; a key frame every 30 samples with\n624\t  float32 absolutes), orientation (smallest-three quaternion, int16), speed (uint8 km/h/2), flags (grounded, boost,\n625\t  brake). ≈ 15 KB per minute; stored base64 in the profile (best run per track, 10 replay slots).\n626\t- Playback: interpolate position (lerp) and orientation (slerp) at any time; wheel spin and steering are derived\n627\t  (speed, yaw rate). Ghost cars draw with `pen.ghost = true` (E3) in a light tint of their paint.\n628\t- A **replay** is a ghost plus metadata (track id or embedded custom track, car, paint, time, date, events with step\n629\t  numbers: CPs, respawns, finish)."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66d97bf5-dd15-40b7-85f8-8eecadfc963f","uuid":"b5c2b193-e726-4a3c-be9e-9f49eabbc43c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:03:27.308Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-050308__x1f94fb/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n### 3.1 The core loop (must feel instant)\n\nTrack select → **flyover** (2.5 s camera sweep along the route with the track name; any button skips) → **3-2-1-GO**\n(start-gate lights, Monsieur Drapeau drops the flag, beeps, gibberish count) → drive → each checkpoint shows the split\nand the delta to your best (blue `-0.42` ahead, red `+0.31` behind) → **FINISH** (slow-mo 0.6 s, camera swings\nround) → results (time, delta, medal drop-in, coppers count-up) → **Retry is one button and takes under half a\nsecond.** In play: **Respawn** puts you at the last checkpoint, standing, the clock still running (TrackMania 2003's\nclassic respawn); **Restart** goes back to the start with a short 1-second \"READY... GO\". Both work at any moment,\nincluding mid-air. The ghost of your best run (translucent) races with you; Coco's ghost (the author time, generated\nby the bot) can be switched on in Settings.\n\n### 3.2 Input maps (`game.input` presets; prompts always from `game.input.label(action)` + our glyph sprites)\n\nRace (`RACE_INPUT`; analog via E4 `input.analog`):\n\n| Action | DualSense (standard mapping) | Keyboard | Notes |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| steer | left stick X (analog), d-pad ←/→ | ←/→, A/D | `input.move()[0]`; keyboard steering ramps (see §4.4 `steerRamp`) |\n| gas | R2 (Pad7, analog), ✕ (Pad0) | ↑, W | analog value 0..1 |\n| brake / reverse | L2 (Pad6, analog), □ (Pad2) | ↓, S | brake + steer at speed = drift (§4.4) |\n| respawn (last CP) | ○ (Pad1) | Enter, Backspace | TrackMania habit |\n| restart (from start) | △ (Pad3) | Delete, R | |\n| camera (far → close → hood) | R1 (Pad5) | C (also 1/2/3 pick one) | |\n| ghost on/off | L1 (Pad4) | G | |\n| horn (just for fun: two-tone toot + gibberish \"beep beep\") | R3 (Pad11) | H | |\n| pause | Options (Pad9) | Esc, P | engine standard |\n\nMouse in races: none (racing doesn't aim); the cursor hides while driving and reappears on menus.\n\nMenus (engine `up/down/left/right/confirm/cancel` + ours): d-pad/left stick move focus; ✕/Enter/Space choose;\n○/Esc/Backspace back; L1/R1 or Q/E switch tabs; △/Y \"secondary\" (e.g. ghost toggle on track select, reset on a\nslider); **mouse hover moves the focus, click chooses, wheel scrolls lists**. Repeat on hold (`input.repeat`).\n\nEditor (`EDIT_INPUT`, §5.4) and replay (`REPLAY_INPUT`, §5.8) have their own tables in their sections.\n\nRumble (`input.rumble`): wall hits (∝ impact), hard landings, boost pads (short), checkpoint (tiny), finish.\n\n**AI Hub reserved:** in a session, ignore Options (pause) while Create (Pad8) is held.\n\n### 3.3 10-foot UI rules (apply everywhere)\n\n- Buffer is `res: 'ps1', expand: true` (~427×240 on 16:9). Primary text: pixel font at **scale 2** (14 px of 240 ≈\n  6% of screen height). Secondary text scale 1, never the `tiny` font for anything the player must read. Big numbers\n  (timer, speed) use a custom chunky digit sprite at 2–3× (§7.6).\n- Tiles at least 96×64 buffer px, 8 px gaps, 12 px safe margins (and keep clear of the engine's top-right corner\n  buttons: `game.cornerArea()`).\n- One focused element always visible (accent border + 1.08× scale tween + a soft glow); spatial navigation; hover =\n  focus; click = choose. Every screen has a back path (○/Esc/right-click).\n- A **prompt bar** along the bottom of every screen: `[glyph] Select  [glyph] Back  [glyph] ...` — glyphs follow\n  `input.lastDevice` (PlayStation shapes by default; Xbox letters if the Settings \"Button symbols\" is Xbox; keycaps\n  for keyboard; mouse icons when the mouse was last used).\n- No dense data screens: at most 6 numbers on any results/records panel; lists show 5–7 rows at scale 2 with\n  scrolling.\n- Colour is never the only signal (deltas carry `+`/`−`, medals carry letters B/S/G/A on their icons).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Core systems\n\n### 4.1 Blocks (the catalogue)\n\nEvery track — campaign, puzzle, editor — is a list of placements `{ type, cx, cy, L, rot }` (rot = heading of the\nblock's local +x: 0 E, 1 S, 2 W, 3 N). In its **local frame** a block's entry is the centre of the west face of local\ncell (0,0) at level 0, heading +x; local y is to the right (south when rot = 0). Footprint offsets below are\n`(along, right, levels)`.\n\n| Type | Token | Footprint (along × right × levels) | Exit (local cell, heading) | Geometry | Surface | Cost (¢) | Envs |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Start | `ST` | 1×1×1 | (1,0) → +x | straight; spawn at s = 8 m; start arch at s = 10 m | road | 0 (max 1) | all |\n| Finish | `FN` | 1×1×1 | (1,0) → +x | straight; finish arch at s = 16 m | road | 0 (≥1) | all |\n| Checkpoint | `CP` | 1×1×1 | (1,0) | straight; gate at s = 16 m | road | 15 | all |\n| Straight | `S` | 1×1×1 | (1,0) | straight | road | 5 | all |\n| Boost | `BO` | 1×1×1 | (1,0) | straight + boost pad (s 10–22 m) | road+boost | 40 | all |\n| Turn, tight | `L1`/`R1` | 1×1×1 | side cell | quarter circle r = 16 m | road | 8 | all |\n| Turn, wide | `L2`/`R2` | 2×2×1 | (1, ±2) heading ±y | quarter circle r = 48 m | road | 15 | all |\n| Turn, sweeping | `L3`/`R3` | 3×3×1 | (2, ±3) heading ±y | quarter circle r = 80 m | road | 25 | all |\n| Banked turn | `BL2`/`BR2` | 2×2×2 | as L2/R2 | r = 48 m, bank 0→28°→0 (sin ramp) | road | 30 | Dustbowl, Frostpeak |\n| Hill up/down (steep) | `U1`/`D1` | 1×1×2 | (1,0), level ±1 | smoothstep rise 8 m over 32 m (max grade 37.5%: launches you at speed) | road | 10 | all |\n| Hill up/down | `U2`/`D2` | 2×1×2 | (2,0), level ±1 | smoothstep rise 8 m over 64 m (max 18.75%) | road | 15 | all |\n| Kicker | `KI` | 1×1×2 | none (air) | concave arc to a **15° lip, 4.2 m high** at s = 32 m (arc radius 123.6 m) | road | 30 | all |\n| Landing | `LA` | 2×1×2 | (2,0) | air entry; smoothstep descent from +3 m to 0 over 64 m | road | 20 | all |\n| Gap | `GAPn` | n×1×2 reserved air | — | nothing (a reserved corridor); the track's **chasm** list (default: its level-0 GAP cells) cuts the base plate | — | 0 | all |\n| Loop | `LOOPR`/`LOOPL` | 2×2×4 | (2, ±1) → +x | §4.2: 12 m-radius loop with a one-cell sideways shift; lane assist | road | 120 | all |\n| Crossing | `CR` | 1×1×1 | all four faces | flat square deck, 4 ports | road | 20 | all |\n| Bumps | `BU` | 1×1×1 | (1,0) | three 0.5 m humps (`z = 0.5·sin²(3πs/32)`) | road | 10 | Hedgerow |\n| Dirt straight / turns | `DS`, `DL1`/`DR1`, `DL2`/`DR2` | as S / L1 / L2 | | | dirt | as base | Hedgerow, Dustbowl |\n| Ice straight / turns | `IS`, `IL1`/`IR1`, `IL2`/`IR2` | as S / L1 / L2 | | | ice | as base | Frostpeak |\n| Deco items | (editor only) | 1×1 | — | scenery props from §7.4 | — | 5–25 | per env |\n\nTurtle rules (§6.1) for where the next block goes follow from the \"Exit\" column: a turn of size n fills the n×n square\n`c0 + a·h + b·s` (a, b ∈ [0, n)) and exits into `c0 + (n−1)·h + n·s` heading `s` (s = the turn side); a loop fills a\n2×2×4 box and exits into `c0 + 2h + s` with the heading unchanged; hills occupy their cells on both levels they span;\na kicker reserves the level above its cell; `GAPn` reserves n cells on levels L and L+1.\n\n**Ports and links.** A port = (world cell, face, level, heading). Two blocks connect when a port of one and a port of\nthe other share the face, level, and opposite headings. Straight-like blocks are symmetric (drivable both ways); turns,\nhills, kickers, landings, loops, start and finish are directional for the route (a car can still drive them\nbackwards physically). **Jump links:** a kicker links to the first landing (or any block whose entry faces it) found\nalong its heading within 5 cells, on the kicker's level or up to 3 levels lower. The **route** is the chain of links\nfrom Start to Finish (§4.8); the editor shows unlinked ports as red arrows.\n\n### 4.2 Block paths (centrelines and frames)\n\nEach block type exports `path(s) -> { p, t, u }` for s ∈ [0, len] in local metres (p position, t unit tangent, u unit\nup), plus `width(s)`, `bank`, and `surface(s)`. Right is `r = u × t`. Formulas (local frame, entry at (0,0,0), +x\nforward, +y right):\n\n- **Straight** (n cells): `p = (s, 0, 0)`, `t = (1,0,0)`, `u = (0,0,1)`, `len = 32n`.\n- **Turn R, radius ρ = 32n − 16** (n = 1, 2, 3): `φ = s/ρ`, `p = (ρ sin φ, ρ(1 − cos φ), 0)`, `t = (cos φ, sin φ, 0)`,\n  `len = πρ/2`. L mirrors y. Check: n = 1 exits at (16, 16) — the centre of the south face of cell (0,0).\n- **Banked**: as the turn; bank `β(φ) = 28°·sin(2φ)` (0 at both ports, 28° mid-bend); `u = cos β·ẑ + sin β·r̂_in` where `r̂_in` points to the\n  turn centre (right for R). The road edge on the outside rises; the ports stay flat.\n- **Hill Un** (rise H = 8 m over len = 32n): `z(s) = H·(3x² − 2x³)`, x = s/len; `t ∝ (1, 0, z'(s))`;\n  `u ∝ (−z'(s), 0, 1)`. D mirrors (descends). The U1 crest has radius ≈ 21 m: above ~60 km/h the car takes off (by\n  design); U2's crest (≈ 85 m) holds the car up to ~150 km/h.\n- **Kicker**: `z(s) = ρk − sqrt(ρk² − s²)`, ρk = 123.6 m, s ∈ [0, 32]: lip angle 15°, lip height 4.2 m.\n- **Landing**: `z(s) = 3·(1 − (3x² − 2x³))`, x = s/64.\n- **Loop R** (exit one cell right, two cells ahead, same heading). Let `S = 32 + 2π·12 + 32` (≈ 139.4 m) be the\n  total centreline length and `y(s) = 32·(3q² − 2q³)` with q = s/S (the sideways shift spread over the whole piece).\n  For s ∈ [0, 32]: `p = (s, y, 0)`; for the circle (θ = (s − 32)/12 ∈ [0, 2π]): `p = (32 + 12 sin θ, y, 12(1 − cos θ))`,\n  `u0 = (−sin θ, 0, cos θ)`; for s ∈ [32 + 24π, S]: `p = (32 + (s − 32 − 24π), y, 0)` — i.e. the circle's bottom is at\n  local x = 32, entering and leaving there, shifted sideways. Tangent = normalized derivative (numerical, h = 0.01 m);\n  up = `u0` Gram–Schmidt'ed against t. At the circle's bottom points the entry and exit lanes are ~23 m apart, more\n  than a road width, so the ribbons never touch. L mirrors y. The loop block has **lane assist** (§4.4 step 7).\n- **Crossing**: a flat 32×32 m deck; its \"path\" for routing is the straight line through the two opposite ports the\n  route uses.\n\nPort frames must match exactly between linked blocks (position within 1 cm, tangent and up within 0.5°): a test checks\nevery link of every shipped track (§9).\n\n### 4.3 Geometry, materials and colliders\n\n**Ribbon mesher.** Sample each block path every 1 m (curves) or per cell (straights; 4 segments), and at each sample\nlay the environment's **cross-section** (a list of (lateral offset, height, uv.u, part) points) along `r` and `u`.\nParts: `road`, `line` (baked into the road texture), `curb`, `rail` (vertical barrier), `bank` (snowbank / hedge /\nstone wall), `underside`. Output per part: render triangles (three winding) + UVs (u across in metres/2, v along in\nmetres/4 so the pixel textures tile at ~8–12 cm per texel) and collision triangles (Rapier winding, engine units) with a\nsurface tag.\n\n| Env | Road width | Curb | Elevated edge | Ground-level edge | Supports under elevated pieces |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Dustbowl | 14 m asphalt, yellow centre dashes, white edges | 1 m red/white, +0.2 m, drivable | steel guard rail 0.9 m (solid) | sand (base plate) | concrete pillars 1.4 m square every 16 m along both edges |\n| Hedgerow | 12 m tarmac (or dirt), white edges | 0.8 m white/green | low stone wall 0.8 m (solid) | grass verge; hedges on some pieces (deco) | earth embankment (45° grassy slopes, drivable, slow) |\n| Frostpeak | 12 m packed-snow road (or ice), orange edge poles every 8 m (deco) | 0.8 m blue/white | snowbank 1.2 m (sloped, low grip: pushes you back) | snow | rock-and-snow embankment |\n\n- Turns and banked turns get the elevated-edge barrier on their **outer** edge even at ground level (Dustbowl: tyre\n  wall instead of rail).\n- Loops get 0.5 m lips both sides. Kickers and landings get curbs only. Gaps get nothing.\n- **Base plate** (per track): one mesh of the grid's cells minus the track's chasm cells (§6.3); environment ground\n  texture (sand ripples / mown grass stripes / snow with sparkles). Collider: one trimesh, surface = the env's\n  off-road surface. **Chasm walls**: for each chasm cell edge that borders plate, a vertical quad down 60 m with the\n  terrain rock texture (canyons) or down 2 m to a water surface mesh (streams, ponds; water is a `water` trigger). **Boundary**: a 2 m wall all round the grid (Dustbowl: striped concrete barriers; Hedgerow: dry\n  stone wall; Frostpeak: snow fence) with a collider.\n- **Materials** (made once per world at boot): `MeshLambertNodeMaterial({ map })` for road/curb/ground/supports with\n  the baked textures (`NearestFilter`, repeat, sRGB) — this matches the engine's level look; walls/rails/props in\n  `MeshToonNodeMaterial({ map, gradientMap: World3D.TOON_BANDS })` (E6). Track meshes are environment (not added to\n  `world._obj`), so the \"objects\" filter mode leaves them alone. Cast/receive shadows on all track meshes.\n- **Gates, boards, boost chevrons, edge poles, flags** are drawn with `world.pen` every frame (animated; a few dozen\n  parts each). Gate posts also get box colliders.\n- **Colliders** live in `TrackPhysics`'s own `RAPIER.World` (gravity irrelevant, never stepped with bodies; call\n  `pw.step()` once after adding/removing colliders so queries see them). One trimesh collider per block (road + curbs\n  + lips + underside) tagged with its surface(s) — if a block mixes surfaces (boost pad), split it into one collider\n  per surface. Barriers/walls as separate trimesh colliders tagged `wall`. `Map(collider.handle → { blockId, surface })`.\n- Rapier 0.19.3 JS facts verified while planning: `castRayAndGetNormal(ray, maxToi, solid, flags, groups,\n  excludeCollider, excludeBody)` → `{ timeOfImpact, normal, collider, featureType, featureId }` (camelCase);\n  `castShape(pos, rot, vel, shape, targetDistance, maxToi, stopAtPenetration, ...)` → `{ time_of_impact, witness1,\n  witness2, normal1, normal2, collider }` (snake_case `time_of_impact`); `projectPoint(p, solid)` → `{ point,\n  isInside, collider, ... }`; `intersectionsWithShape(pos, rot, shape, cb)`. Take a wall normal as `normal2` flipped,\n  if needed, so it opposes the motion.\n\n### 4.4 The car (validated model — build exactly this, then tune with Dev Mode)\n\nThe car is **not** a physics body. Each step (1/120 s) it probes the track with four wheel rays, follows the surface\nit's on with velocity-level constraints, and flies ballistically when the surface can't hold it. This is what makes\nloops hold when you're fast and drop you when you're slow — TrackMania's feel — and it's deterministic.\n\nState (engine units): `p` (chassis reference point: centre of the wheelbase, `ride` above the road), `v`, frame\n`f, u` (r derived), `grounded`, `n` (surface normal last step), `kappa` (filtered curvature), `load` (normal load per\nunit mass), `slip` (detach timer),\n`air` (seconds airborne), `flop` (crash-recovery timer), `boostT`, `drift`, `surface`, `blockId`, per-wheel `d` (for\ndrawing suspension), `steerVis`, `slide` (for FX/sound), `impact` (last impact speed).\n\n```text\nstep(car, ctl{steer -1..1, gas 0..1, brake 0..1}, dt):\n  g = (0, 0, -G)                                   G = CFG.gravity (default 1.5 g = 14.7 m/s²)\n  1 PROBE: for each wheel mount m_i = p + f·lx_i + r·ly_i (lx = ±wheelbase/2, ly = ±track/2):\n       origin = m_i + u·0.5 m; ray along −u, length 0.5 m + ride + reach (reach = 0.9 m)\n       hit -> point_i, normal_i, d_i = toi − 0.5 m, surface_i (collider map)\n  2 SURFACE: if 4 hits: n = normalize(cross(FR − RL, FL − RR)), flipped to agree with u   (plane through the\n       contacts: smooth on a faceted mesh — averaging triangle normals made the car let go at the top of the loop)\n     else if ≥ 2 hits: n = normalize(Σ normal_i); else no surface.  d̄ = mean d_i.\n  3 CONTACT:\n     if n:\n       vn = v·n;  pull = g·n  (> 0: gravity pulls the car off this surface)\n       if grounded: k0 = −((n − car.n)·v̂) / max(1, |v|·dt);  car.kappa += (k0 − car.kappa)·min(1, dt/0.04)\n       else car.kappa = 0\n       vt2 = |v|² − vn²;  Aeff = A·min(1, sqrt(vt2) / 15 m/s)   A = CFG.adhesion (0.35 g), fading out at low speed\n       load = vt2·car.kappa − pull + Aeff                         (normal load per unit mass; ≥ 0: the surface holds you)\n       car.slip = load >= 0 ? 0 : car.slip + dt\n       stay = grounded ? (car.slip < 0.06 s && d̄ < ride + reach)\n                       : (vn < 0 && d̄ < ride + 0.6·reach)        (landing)\n     grounded = n && stay\n  4 GROUNDED:\n     if just landed: impact = −vn; if u·n < 0.3 -> FLOP (step 8); else v −= n·vn,\n                     v *= 1 − clamp((impact − 6 m/s)·0.02, 0, 0.25); landing FX (dust ring, thump, shake ∝ impact)\n     u = normalize(u + (n − u)·min(1, 30·dt));  f = normalize(f − u(f·u));  r = u × f\n     v −= n(v·n)                                                  (no motion into or off the surface)\n     s = v·f\n     a = g − n(g·n)                                               (gravity along the surface: slopes matter)\n     traction = surface.grip·max(0, load)                         (what the tyres can pass on: μ·N/m)\n     gas:   if s < vtop: a += f·min(traction, gas·A0·(1 − (max(s,0)/vtop)^1.6))\n     brake: if s > 0.5 m/s: a −= v̂·min(traction, brake·B) (clamp so v doesn't reverse this step)\n            else: a −= f·min(traction, brake·Arev) while s > −vrev   (reverse)\n     coast: if gas = 0: a −= v̂·1.2 m/s²;  rolling: a −= v̂·surface.roll;  aero: a −= v·cd·|v|\n     boost: if boostT > 0: a += f·CFG.boostAccel; boostT −= dt\n     steering (bicycle model): δmax = lerp(δlo, δhi, clamp(|s|/vtop, 0, 1)^0.7)\n       steerIn: keyboard input ramps to ±1 over 0.12 s and back over 0.08 s; sticks apply directly (deadzone by engine)\n       drift = brake > 0.5 && |steer| > 0.5 && s > 60 km/h (TrackMania's brake-drift)\n       yawRate = s·tan(steer·δmax)/wheelbase·(drift ? 1.3 : 1)\n       f = rotate(f, about u, yawRate·dt); r = u × f\n     grip: vlat = v·r; maxDv = grip·surface.grip·(load/G)·(drift ? driftGrip : 1)·dt   (= the tuned grip on flat\n           ground; more when pressed into a loop or bank, less over a crest or upside down)\n           dv = clamp(−vlat, −maxDv, maxDv); v += r·dv; slide = |vlat| − |dv|\n     v += a·dt;  p += v·dt;  p += n·(ride − d̄)·min(1, 25·dt)        (ride-height spring on position)\n     car.n = n;  surface = most common surface_i;  boost pad: entering a boost collider while grounded ->\n       v += f·CFG.boostDv (cap at 1.3·vtop), boostT = CFG.boostTime (re-arm after leaving that pad)\n  5 AIRBORNE:\n     v += g·dt;  v −= v·cdAir·|v|·dt;  p += v·dt;  air += dt\n     f = rotate(f, about u, ctl.steer·airYaw·dt)                  (air steering)\n     f = normalize(f + (v̂ − f)·min(1, 1.5·dt)); r = normalize(u × f); u = normalize(f × r)   (nose follows the arc)\n     u = normalize(u + (ẑ − u)·min(1, 0.8·dt)), re-orthonormalize   (gentle roll levelling: no side landings after a\n                                                                       mistimed loop)\n  6 WALLS (both states, after moving): cast the chassis box (half extents L/2, W/2, 0.45 m; centre p + u·0.35 m;\n     rotation from (f, r, u)) from the old to the new position with castShape (targetDistance 0.02 m). Ignore hits\n     whose normal nw has |nw·u| > 0.65 (that's ground, step 3 owns it). On a wall hit: move to the contact\n     (time_of_impact), vN = v·nw; v −= nw·vN·(1 + e) (e = 0.15); v *= 1 − 0.1·min(1, |vN|/10);\n     turn f toward the wall tangent by up to 0.25 rad; slide the remaining motion once more; sparks at witness1;\n     scrape sound while touching; |vN| > 15 m/s = crash (shake, rumble, big sparks). If the box starts overlapping\n     a wall (intersectionsWithShape), restore the previous p and remove the inward velocity.\n  7 LANE ASSIST (only on blocks with assist: loops): find the nearest centreline sample of the current block, lateral\n     error e (along r) and its rate; f = rotate(f, about u, clamp(−0.35·e/1m − 0.08·ė/(1 m/s), −1, 1)·1.2·dt).\n     CFG.loopAssist (on by default; a Setting and a Dev slider) scales it.\n  8 FLOP: when landing on the side/roof (u·n < 0.3) or stuck upside down: 0.6 s animation that rotates the car\n     upright onto the surface below, v *= 0.3, inputs ignored. Cartoonish, keeps flow; respawn is still one button.\n  9 OUT OF BOUNDS: p.z < −25 m (fell into a chasm or off the world) -> auto-respawn after a 0.4 s fade.\n```\n\nPrototype results (headless, Rapier 0.19.3 trimesh ribbons, Appendix A's code exactly as printed: Coyote tuning,\nG = 1.5 g, adhesion 0.35 g, ride 0.55 m, reach 0.9 m): **12 m loop on full throttle** — 40 km/h entry drops off the\ntop, 47 km/h holds (46 km/h over the top), 59–102 km/h hold; **coasting** — 101 km/h drops off, 107 km/h holds;\n**15° kicker, 64 m gap, landing pad from +3 m** — 135 km/h at the lip falls into the gap, 161 / 181 / 194 km/h land\nupright 9 / 29 / 45 m into the pad after 1.65–2.07 s of air. Two lessons from the spike: averaging triangle normals\ninstead of the four-point plane made the car let go on every flat facet of the loop (keep the plane fit); without\ntraction limits the engine pushed the car up the loop from any speed (keep `traction`). In a full-course run with a\nsideways-shifted loop (as the loop block has), the car stayed on only with lane assist — keep it on loop blocks.\n\n**Car tuning (defaults; all live in Dev Mode):**\n\n| | Coyote (Dustbowl) | Pebble (Hedgerow) | Moose (Frostpeak) |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Body L×W×H (m) | 4.4 × 1.9 × 1.25 | 3.8 × 1.75 × 1.35 | 4.1 × 1.95 × 1.7 |\n| Wheelbase / track / wheel radius (m) | 2.7 / 1.6 / 0.36 | 2.4 / 1.5 / 0.32 | 2.5 / 1.65 / 0.45 |\n| ride (m) | 0.55 | 0.50 | 0.70 |\n| vtop | 230 km/h | 195 km/h | 175 km/h |\n| A0 (accel at 0) / B (brake) / Arev, vrev | 12 / 24 m/s² / 6, 40 km/h | 14 / 28 / 6, 40 | 11 / 22 / 6, 40 |\n| δlo / δhi (steer at 0 / top speed) | 34° / 7° | 36° / 9° | 32° / 9° |\n| grip (lateral, asphalt) | 15 m/s² | 18 m/s² | 14 m/s² |\n| driftGrip | 0.55 | 0.70 | 0.60 |\n| airYaw | 1.2 rad/s | 1.5 rad/s | 1.0 rad/s |\n| cd / cdAir | 0.0004 /m | 0.0004 | 0.0005 |\n| adhesion | 0.35 g | 0.35 g | 0.40 g |\n\nGlobal: gravity 1.5 g; boostDv 10 m/s; boostAccel 7 m/s²; boostTime 1.2 s; wall e 0.15.\n\n**Surfaces** (`grip` multiplier per car, `roll` = rolling resistance m/s²):\n\n| Surface | Coyote | Pebble | Moose | roll | FX / sound |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| road (asphalt / tarmac / packed snow road) | 1.0 | 1.0 | 1.0 | 0.15 | tyre squeal |\n| dirt | 0.75 | 0.95 | 0.85 | 0.6 | brown dust, crunch |\n| grass (verge, embankment) | 0.55 | 0.60 | 0.65 | 2.5 | green bits |\n| sand (Dustbowl plate) | 0.50 | 0.55 | 0.60 | 4.0 | sand plume |\n| snow (Frostpeak plate, snowbank) | 0.60 | 0.65 | 0.90 | 1.2 | snow spray |\n| ice | 0.30 | 0.35 | 0.55 | 0.05 | ice hiss, sparkles |\n| boost | as road | | | 0.15 | chevrons flash |\n\n### 4.5 Cameras (`car/camera.js`; all through `world.camera` in `'fixed'` mode with `up`, E2)\n\nSet `world.camera.mouseLook = false` (no pointer lock in races). Compute in steps, place in `onDraw` interpolated with\n`game.alpha` (the engine leaves a pose set in `onDraw` to the game).\n- **Far chase (default):** target `T = p + u·1.2 m + f·3 m`; smoothed frame `fc` (forward) and `uc` (up) chase the\n  car's `f, u` at 6/s and 4/s while grounded; in the air `fc` follows `v̂` and `uc` eases to ẑ at 1.5/s (the camera\n  doesn't spin with flips). Position `T − fc·(6.5 m + 0.012 s·|v|) + uc·2.0 m`. FOV 70° + 12°·clamp((kmh − 100)/150,\n  0, 1) + 6° while boosting (reduce-motion: no FOV kick). If a ray from T to the camera hits the track, pull in.\n- **Close chase:** 4.2 m back, 1.3 m up, FOV 75°. **Hood:** `p + f·0.6 + u·1.15`, look along f, up u, FOV 80°; the\n  pen draws the bonnet and a dashboard strip (the overlay pen, as the shooter kit draws a gun) so it reads as a car.\n- **Flyover (intro):** samples the route; the camera rides 25 m above and 30 m beside the route from start to finish\n  over 2.5 s (smoothstep), then cuts behind the car.\n- **Finish orbit:** 10 m radius around the car, 0.35 rad/s, slight slow-motion (`game.timeScale = .35` for 0.6 s).\n- **TV (replays):** trackside spots generated along the route every ~5 blocks, 25 m to the side and 6 m up; the\n  nearest spot with a clear line of sight films; FOV narrows to keep the car ~1/4 of screen height.\n- **Orbit/free (replays, results):** right stick / mouse drag orbit, triggers / wheel zoom.\n- **Editor:** orbit around the cursor (yaw, pitch 25°–80°, distance 60–400 m), smoothed (§5.4).\n- Split screen: one `world.addCamera()` per extra viewport, each with its own chase state.\n\n### 4.6 A run (`race/run.js`)\n\n- Phases: `intro` (flyover) → `countdown` (3 s; 1 s on restart) → `racing` → `finished` | `abandoned`.\n- The clock counts **steps** from GO; the car is held (brakes on, gas revs the engine sound only) before GO.\n- **Gates:** each CP/finish gate is a plane (point, normal = path tangent, half-width = road half-width + 1 m,\n  height 7 m above the road along u). A crossing = the segment from the previous to the new car position crosses\n  the plane within those bounds. **Checkpoints count once each, in any order, either direction** (TrackMania).\n  **Finish counts only forward and only with every checkpoint passed**; otherwise show \"MISSING CHECKPOINT\" once.\n- **Respawn:** to the last checkpoint passed (or the start): car at the gate (or spawn) frame, `v = 0`, upright,\n  `boostT = 0`; the clock keeps running; respawn counter +1; warp-in FX (glints, a quick scale-in, rising arpeggio).\n- **Restart:** new run object; ghost recording restarts; respawn counter 0.\n- **Splits:** per run, the step count at each CP in the order passed; compare to the best run's splits (by order).\n- Events emitted for HUD/sound/FX: `cp(i, steps, delta)`, `finish(steps, delta, medal)`, `respawn`, `restart`,\n  `boost`, `land(impact)`, `wall(impact)`, `flop`, `missingCp`.\n\n### 4.7 Ghosts and replays (`race/ghost.js`)\n\n- Record every 4th step (30 Hz): position (int16 deltas in 1/16 unit — 1/256 m; a key frame every 30 samples with\n  float32 absolutes), orientation (smallest-three quaternion, int16), speed (uint8 km/h/2), flags (grounded, boost,\n  brake). ≈ 15 KB per minute; stored base64 in the profile (best run per track, 10 replay slots).\n- Playback: interpolate position (lerp) and orientation (slerp) at any time; wheel spin and steering are derived\n  (speed, yaw rate). Ghost cars draw with `pen.ghost = true` (E3) in a light tint of their paint.\n- A **replay** is a ghost plus metadata (track id or embedded custom track, car, paint, time, date, events with step\n  numbers: CPs, respawns, finish).","numLines":330,"startLine":300,"totalLines":1464}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01H3i2sTfb6S36toz1bvK5kA","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghrZ1MB9uGSYutXWsiAX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011besEUKboWSCdmPoLzp18e","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-050308__x1f94fb/work/PLAN.md","offset":630,"limit":300},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13455,"cache_read_input_tokens":35915,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13455},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66d97bf5-dd15-40b7-85f8-8eecadfc963f","uuid":"3ae51def-ee75-459a-b6bd-c4a5024cbfcd","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:03:33.116Z","request_id":"req_011CghrZ16JEtLeL5sUdgyHE","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_011besEUKboWSCdmPoLzp18e":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-050308__x1f94fb/work/PLAN.md","offset":630,"limit":300}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011besEUKboWSCdmPoLzp18e","type":"tool_result","content":"630\t- Coco's ghost (author run) is not stored: regenerate it by running the bot (deterministic, ~0.2 s) when needed.\n631\t\n632\t### 4.8 The autopilot (`race/bot.js`) — used by tests, medal baking, Survival rivals, attract mode, Dev Mode\n633\t\n634\t1. **Route:** walk links from Start's exit port to Finish, following each block's path in the traversed direction\n635\t   and jump links over gaps; crossings go straight through. Sample every 2 m: `{ p, t, u, r, halfWidth (road/2 −\n636\t   1.2 m), surface, flags: kicker|landing|loop|boost|gate, block }`. A route that doesn't reach Finish is an editor\n637\t   error (\"Route broken at ...\").\n638\t2. **Racing line:** lateral offsets e_i ∈ [−hw, +hw], start at 0, 80 iterations of curvature smoothing with clamping\n639\t   (`e_i ← clamp(e_i + 0.5·((e_{i−1} + e_{i+1})/2 − e_i) − 0.3·κ_i·hw, −hw, hw)`, κ signed in the surface plane); force\n640\t   e = 0 on loops, kickers, landings, gates and boost pads (the line goes through pads).\n641\t3. **Speed profile:** `vmax_i = min(vtop·1.3, sqrt(a_lat / |κ_i|))`, a_lat = skillGrip·grip·surfaceGrip (+ g·sin(bank)\n642\t   on banks); full speed through loops and kickers; then a backward pass with braking B·skillBrake and a forward pass\n643\t   with the car's acceleration curve. Flag tracks where the speed before a kicker is below what its gap needs\n644\t   (`v ≥ sqrt(g·gapLength/sin(30°))`·1.1) — a test fails on that.\n645\t4. **Control (each step):** nearest route index (search a ±15-sample window after the last one, by 3D distance — never\n646\t   jump between a loop's two lanes); lookahead point at `6 m + 0.35 s·|v|`; α = angle to it in the car's (f, r)\n647\t   plane; `steer = clamp(1.6·α/δmax(v))`; `gas = 1` if v < target − 0.5 m/s; `brake = clamp((v − target)/5)` if\n648\t   v > target + 1 m/s; in the air: steer 0, gas 1.\n649\t5. **Recovery:** off the route by more than hw + 3 m for 0.6 s, slower than 1 m/s for 1.5 s after GO, or two flops in\n650\t   a row → respawn.\n651\t6. **Skill 0..1:** grip use 0.75 + 0.25·skill, brake margin ×(1.25 − 0.25·skill), lookahead jitter ±0.4 m·(1 −\n652\t   skill) from `E.rng(seed)`, a lazy line (e scaled by 0.6 + 0.4·skill). Skill 1, no cheats = the **author** driver.\n653\t7. **Cheats (attract/demo only):** lane snap (pull p toward the line, 4 m/s max), +10% grip, auto-respawn instantly.\n654\t\n655\t### 4.9 Medals (`race/medals.js`, `tools/bake.mjs`)\n656\t\n657\t- Author time = the bot at skill 1 without cheats (campaign and puzzle reference solutions), baked by\n658\t  `node tools/bake.mjs` into `src/data/medals.json` (`{ id: { author, gold, silver, bronze } }` in steps). Re-bake\n659\t  after any tuning change (Dev Mode has \"Re-bake this track\" for live tuning; tests fail if a baked value no longer\n660\t  matches a fresh bot run within 1 step).\n661\t- **Gold = author × 1.06 rounded up to 0.1 s; Silver = × 1.2 rounded up to 1 s; Bronze = × 1.5 rounded up to 1 s**\n662\t  (TrackMania's ratios). Multipliers are Dev sliders; a track may carry `medalScale` to adjust.\n663\t- Editor tracks: author = your validation time; the same ratios.\n664\t- Medal icons carry letters (B, S, G, A). The Author medal is \"Coco's Time\".\n665\t\n666\t---\n667\t\n668\t## 5. Modes and features\n669\t\n670\t### 5.1 Profile, progression and the coppers economy (`save/profile.js`, `modes/campaign.js`)\n671\t\n672\tProfile (one per browser; `E.store` key `crackmania:profile`, `version: 1`, with a `migrate()` hook): name (letter\n673\twheel), coppers, per-track records `{ bestSteps, bestSplits, medal: 0..4, ghost, attempts }`, puzzle records, survival\n674\tbest rank per gauntlet, unlocked packs and patterns, garage paint per car, 6 custom track slots, 10 replay slots, seen\n675\tstory beats, first-time tips seen. In AI Hub sessions the hub gives the page empty, temporary storage: nothing to do.\n676\t\n677\t**Coppers (¢).** Start with **300 ¢**. Rewards are paid **once per medal tier** (earning Gold first time pays Bronze +\n678\tSilver + Gold):\n679\t\n680\t| | Bronze | Silver | Gold | Author |\n681\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n682\t| Race (× env: Dustbowl 1, Hedgerow 1.25, Frostpeak 1.5) | 60 | 90 | 150 | 300 |\n683\t| Puzzle | 80 | 120 | 200 | 300 |\n684\t\n685\tSurvival: 50 ¢ per round survived beyond your previous best for that gauntlet, plus 300 ¢ the first time a gauntlet is\n686\tcleared. Dev slider: copper multiplier.\n687\t\n688\t**Spending.** Editor blocks cost coppers when placed (refunded 100% when removed; table §4.1). Editor **packs** unlock\n689\tfamilies of blocks: BASIC (start, finish, checkpoint, straights, turns, hills, crossing) free; STUNTS (kicker, landing,\n690\tboost, bumps) 250 ¢; LOOPS & BANKS 600 ¢; SURFACES (dirt and ice variants) 200 ¢; SCENERY 150 ¢. Garage patterns:\n691\t3 free, the other 5 at 100 ¢ each. Prices show on every tile; \"Not enough coppers\" plays the error buzz and shakes the\n692\twallet.\n693\t\n694\t**Unlocks.**\n695\t- Dustbowl D1 and D2 open at start; each next track opens when the previous one has any medal.\n696\t- An environment's **Puzzles** open when its 2nd race has a medal; its **Survival** when its 3rd race has a medal.\n697\t- **Hedgerow** opens with medals on 3 Dustbowl races; **Frostpeak** with medals on 3 Hedgerow races.\n698\t- Build, Hot Seat, Split Screen, Garage and Replays are open from the start (MP modes offer every track of unlocked\n699\t  environments plus custom tracks).\n700\t- Story beats fire on these events (§8.2). Golds on all 15 race tracks trigger the ending and the credits roll.\n701\t\n702\t### 5.2 Race (campaign)\n703\t\n704\tFront end: **Environment select** (three big cards with the car, the env emblem, medal count `G 3/5`, a lock with the\n705\trequirement) → **Track select** (5 tiles: number, name, a baked minimap of the route, best time, medal icon, lock;\n706\t△ toggles \"race Coco's ghost\") → run (§4.6) → **Results** (time big; best and delta; medal drop-in with sting; next\n707\tmedal target \"SILVER 0:31\"; coppers count-up; buttons **Retry** (△ / R), **Next track** (✕ / Enter), **Replay** (□ /\n708\tV), **Save replay**, **Menu** (○ / Esc)). Pause menu items in races: Resume, Restart, Respawn, Camera, Ghosts,\n709\t**Dev Mode**, Settings, Controls, Quit to menu (`menu.items` may be a function; check the engine's `v(...)` wrapper\n710\tand return per-scene items).\n711\t\n712\tHUD (`ui/hud.js`, per viewport): top centre timer `0:23.41` (big digits); under it, for 2 s after a CP, the split and\n713\tdelta; top left `CP 1/3` with a flag icon and the respawn count if > 0; top right the next medal target with its icon\n714\t(and \"BEST 0:31.20\" under it); bottom right speed (big digits + `KM/H`, or MPH by setting) and a boost flame icon while\n715\tboosting; centre: countdown digits (3 → 2 → 1 → GO!, scale 6, pop tween), \"MISSING CHECKPOINT\", \"FINISH!\", \"NEW\n716\tRECORD!\". Bottom centre after a flop or when stopped for 2 s: prompt `○ Respawn  △ Restart`. Edge vignette + speed\n717\tlines above 200 km/h (reduce-motion: off).\n718\t\n719\t### 5.3 Puzzle (`modes/puzzle.js`; runs inside the editor scene)\n720\t\n721\tA puzzle = environment, **fixed blocks** (start, checkpoints, finish; sometimes more), a **build zone** (rectangle of\n722\tcells and levels), **no-build cells** (chasms, hedges, rocks, a pond — drawn as such), an **inventory** (block type →\n723\tcount) and a reference solution (for its author time and for tests). The editor runs in puzzle mode: the palette shows\n724\tonly inventory blocks with remaining counts (`R2 ×1`), fixed blocks show a lock and can't be moved, placement outside\n725\tthe zone is refused, no coppers are spent. **Validate** = drive from start through all CPs to finish; medals by time\n726\tagainst the solution's baked thresholds. Several routes are possible; the inventory includes extra pieces so a smarter\n727\troute (a boost, a wider bend) beats the obvious one. First-time Coco tip explains it in three lines.\n728\t\n729\t### 5.4 Build — the track editor (`editor/editor.js`)\n730\t\n731\tOpening: environment and slot select (6 slots with names, env emblem, validated mark and author time) → the editor.\n732\t\n733\tScreen: the 3D track with an **orbit camera** around the cursor; a translucent **grid** at the cursor's level (pen\n734\tbars every cell within 6 cells of the cursor, brighter on the cursor's row/column); the **cursor** (a pulsing cell\n735\toutline + a ghost preview of the selected block, green if it fits, red if it collides / is outside the grid / you\n736\tcan't afford it; small arrows on its ports, blue when they'd link); placed blocks' open ports show red arrows. Top\n737\tbar: track name, env, coppers (or puzzle counts), status chips `START ✓ FINISH ✓ CP 2 ROUTE ✓ VALIDATED 0:41.20`.\n738\tBottom: the **palette** carousel (categories ROADS / TURNS / HILLS / STUNTS / SURFACES / SCENERY as tabs; 48×36 px\n739\ticons baked top-down from each block's geometry; name, cost, lock if the pack isn't owned). Left: a short prompt list.\n740\t\n741\t| Action | DualSense | Keyboard / mouse |\n742\t| --- | --- | --- |\n743\t| move cursor (camera-relative, repeats) | left stick | WASD / arrows; mouse hover picks the cell under the pointer on the cursor's level (ray–plane) |\n744\t| palette item / category | d-pad ←/→ / ↑/↓ | Tab / Shift+Tab categories, 1–9 items, mouse click on a tile |\n745\t| place | ✕ | Space / Enter / left click |\n746\t| remove block under cursor | □ | Delete / Backspace / right click |\n747\t| rotate selected block | R1 (cw) / L1 (ccw) | R / Shift+R / mouse wheel |\n748\t| level up / down | R2 / L2 | E / Q / Shift+wheel / PageUp / PageDown |\n749\t| orbit / tilt camera | right stick | middle-drag or Alt+left-drag; wheel+Ctrl zooms |\n750\t| test drive from Start | △ | T |\n751\t| undo / redo | L3 / R3 | Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y |\n752\t| editor menu | Options | Esc |\n753\t\n754\tEditor menu: Resume, **Validate** (a run from Start; finishing with every CP sets the author time and medals; any\n755\tedit afterwards clears it), Test drive, Save, Save as, Load, Rename (letter wheel), Environment (only when empty),\n756\tShare code (shows a base64url code in a large box; Copy uses `navigator.clipboard` when allowed), Import code (a text\n757\tfield; keyboard paste), Clear track (asks), Dev Mode, Settings, Exit. Test drive returns to the same cursor and\n758\tcamera. Undo/redo stack of 200 operations (place, remove, rotate, rename) with coppers refunded/charged.\n759\t\n760\tRules: one Start (free), at least one Finish (free), any number of CPs; blocks can't overlap (3D occupancy) but can\n761\tsit above others with ≥ 1 level of clearance (supports are generated automatically and never block a lane under\n762\tthem); gaps under kickers are reserved automatically when a kicker is placed (shown hatched). A track is shareable\n763\tand playable in Hot Seat / Split Screen once validated. A Dev Mode button \"Export as content\" prints a `data/tracks.js`\n764\tentry (placements + metadata) — the designer workflow for growing the game later.\n765\t\n766\t### 5.5 Survival (`modes/survival.js`)\n767\t\n768\tPer environment a **gauntlet of 5 rounds** = that environment's race tracks 1→5 (rounds may include tracks not yet\n769\topen in Race: Survival is their preview). Each round: you vs the **Ghost Guild** — Tex Mirage, Mlle Gravillon, Bobo\n770\tYeti — as ghost cars with name tags. Their runs are bot runs generated at round start (behind a 1-second \"WARMING UP\n771\tTHE GHOSTS\" card; deterministic per gauntlet + round): skills `base + 0.03·round + 0.02·rankIndex` with bases 0.78 /\n772\t0.86 / 0.93 and different seeds (Tex jittery-fast, Gravillon clean, Bobo late braker). Place by finish time (DNF after\n773\tthe last rival finishes + 15 s = last). **1st: +2 ranks, 2nd: +1, 3rd: stay, 4th: out.** Ranks: ROOKIE → DRIVER →\n774\tRACER → PILOT → ACE → MANIAC → CRACKMANIAC. Between rounds: standings card with portraits and a rival quip (§8.2).\n775\tClearing round 5 = \"GAUNTLET CLEARED\" + rewards. Best rank per gauntlet is recorded.\n776\t\n777\t### 5.6 Hot Seat and Split Screen (`modes/hotseat.js`, `modes/split.js`)\n778\t\n779\t**Hot Seat** (TrackMania 2003's local mode): 2–8 players (default names PLAYER 1…; letter wheel to rename), attempts\n780\tper turn 1/2/3, a cup of 1–5 tracks (pick or random). Turn order rotates per track. Before each turn a full-screen\n781\tcard \"PASS THE CONTROLLER TO {NAME}\" (Coco babbles; any button when ready). The leader's best run drives as a ghost.\n782\tScoring per track: 10-8-6-5-4-3-2-1 by best time; cup standings after each track; a podium at the end with each\n783\tplayer's car in their paint colour (assign 8 distinct colours).\n784\t\n785\t**Split Screen:** 2–4 players at once. Join screen: each pad presses ✕ or Options to join (`game.allowJoin({ max: 4 })`),\n786\tkeyboard players join with Enter (left half: WASD + F/G/H) or Numpad Enter (right half: arrows + . / ,), per the\n787\tengine's half-keyboard support. Layout `rows` for 2, `grid` for 3–4 (`game.splitScreen(n, { layout })`,\n788\t`world.addCamera()` per extra viewport; filters are off while split — engine rule). Same countdown; cars are ghosts to\n789\teach other (no collisions, TrackMania style). Each viewport has its own HUD; a player who finishes sees their place;\n790\tthe race ends when all finish or 30 s after the first finish. Best of 1 / 3 races.\n791\t\n792\t### 5.7 Online — AI Hub sessions (`modes/online.js`; protocol at `ai-hub/lib/hub/README.md`)\n793\t\n794\tMode **`ghost`**: each player runs their own copy of the round; positions are exchanged so each copy shows the others\n795\tas ghost cars; nothing they do affects your world. This *is* TrackMania online (cars never collide).\n796\t\n797\tHead metas (in the built HTML):\n798\t```html\n799\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n800\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n801\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n802\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"3\">\n803\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Best time in 3 minutes wins; retry as often as you like\">\n804\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"R2/W gas · L2/S brake · stick/arrows steer · Circle/Enter respawn\">\n805\t<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\"><meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1-4\">\n806\t```\n807\tFlow when `AIHub.active` (true from the first line):\n808\t1. Skip title, attract and menus entirely. Boot, then `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4],\n809\t   card: true })`. If `info` is null, run the normal game.\n810\t2. Pick the round's track with `AIHub.rng('track')` from the session list **D1, D2, D3, R1, R2, S1, S2** (the same\n811\t   pick on every copy; the seed changes per round, so rounds rotate tracks); load it.\n812\t3. **Own card** (§ \"The card\" in the README): the track flyover looping, the track name, each player's name in their\n813\t   seat colour (`info.players[].color`: #e8443a, #3b82f6, #22c55e, #f5b700) with a READY tick from the `card` event's\n814\t   `ready` ids, the goal, the controls for this player's device, and the time left (`card.left`). Enter / ✕ / a tap →\n815\t   `AIHub.answer('ready')`; △ (button 3) or M → `AIHub.answer('more')`. The card has no menus and draws no\n816\t   `Math.random` (use `AIHub.rng('card')` for any jitter). Call `AIHub.ready()` once the world is built — no key press.\n817\t4. On `start`, show 3-2-1-GO against `AIHub.time()` (play begins at 0). Then **time attack**: unlimited restarts and\n818\t   respawns; the round clock (3:00 from `AIHub.time() = 0`) shows top centre; your best time top right.\n819\t5. Every ~100 ms send `{ t: 'g', area: trackId, run: runCounter, ms, p: [x, y, z] (rounded 0.1 unit), q: [x, y, z, w]\n820\t   (4 decimals), v: kmh, f: flags }` with `AIHub.send(data, { reliable: false })` (≤ 10/s, well under the 20/s limit,\n821\t   < 200 bytes). On a new best, send `{ t: 'best', ms }` reliably. Receivers buffer 150 ms and interpolate; a ghost\n822\t   whose `area` differs is hidden; show name tags in seat colours (names drawn by the pixel font on canvas — never as\n823\t   HTML).\n824\t6. Each second `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`: with a best, `score = 2e6 − bestMs`, label `BEST 0:42.31`; without,\n825\t   `score = cpsThisRun·1000 + metresAlongRoute`, label `CP 2/3`.\n826\t7. At 3:00 by `AIHub.time()` (or 5 s before `info.limitMs` if that is sooner) — or at once on `time-up` — call `AIHub.result({ time: bestMs })` if you have a finish,\n827\t   else `AIHub.result({ score })`, exactly once, then show \"WAITING FOR THE OTHERS\" with live ghosts. Include `stats:\n828\t   { Runs: n, Respawns: n }`.\n829\t8. On `end`: stop input and sound (`game.audio.mute(true)`, freeze), show the hub's standings line if given.\n830\t9. On `leave`: remove that ghost. If WebGL 2/WebGPU init fails: `AIHub.fail('3D graphics are not available')`.\n831\t10. In a session: no Quit to title, no title/attract/editor/garage, no `alert/confirm/prompt`, no `window.open`, no\n832\t    network except the hub; Options is ignored while Create (Pad8) is held.\n833\tThe Multiplayer menu outside the hub shows an **Online** tile that explains: \"Online races run in AI Hub sessions —\n834\topen CRACKMANIA from AI Hub with friends.\"\n835\t\n836\t### 5.8 Replays (`modes/replay.js`)\n837\t\n838\tFrom results (\"Replay\") or the Replays list (10 slots: track, time, car, date; delete with □). Viewer: the run's\n839\tghost drawn as a normal (opaque) car with its paint, the HUD's timer and CP splits replayed, camera modes **Chase / TV\n840\t/ Orbit** (R1 / C cycles), play/pause (✕ / Space), scrub (left stick or ←/→; hold for 4×), speed 0.25×–4× (L2/R2 or\n841\t−/=), restart (△ / Home), exit (○ / Esc), mouse: drag to orbit, wheel to zoom, click the timeline bar to seek.\n842\tCustom-track replays embed the track.\n843\t\n844\t### 5.9 Garage — paint shop (`modes/garage.js`)\n845\t\n846\tA small **workshop world** (a separate `E.World3D` with a text `level`: brick walls, a car lift, torches, shelves,\n847\tcrates, barrels, a tyre rack — core shapes plus a few custom ones) with a turntable. Pick car (locked cars show a\n848\tsilhouette and the unlock requirement), then: **Body colour**, **Accent colour** (24-swatch grids, plus HSV sliders),\n849\t**Pattern** (Solid, Twin Stripes, Side Stripe, Checker Roof, Flames, Lightning, Number Panel, Two-Tone), **Pattern\n850\tcolour**, **Number** (00–99, drawn on doors and roof with a 3×5 pixel digit font made of thin boxes), **Rims**\n851\t(6 colours), **Helmet colour**. Live preview spins; △ toggles \"lights on\". Saved per car; used in every mode, replays,\n852\thub ghosts (others see their seat colour, you see your paint).\n853\t\n854\t### 5.10 Dev Mode (`ui/dev.js`; pause menu → \"Dev Mode\")\n855\t\n856\tAn overlay panel (left 45% of the screen, game visible and paused, or running in slow motion if chosen) with three\n857\ttabs (L1/R1, Q/E, click):\n858\t- **TOOLS:** Teleport to next / previous checkpoint; Finish now (records the current time); Award medal (B/S/G/A);\n859\t  Unlock everything; +1000 coppers; Reset profile (asks); Bot drives (toggle, skill slider); Re-bake medals for this\n860\t  track; Time scale 0.25× / 0.5× / 1×; Frame step (while paused); Free camera (fly with sticks/WASD); Show probes\n861\t  (wheel rays, contact plane, normal, κ, slip); Show colliders (wireframe of collision triangles, pen bars); Show route\n862\t  and racing line; Show gates; Show FPS and draw stats (`renderer.info`); Jump to (any track / puzzle / gauntlet\n863\t  round / scene by deep link).\n864\t- **TUNING:** live sliders with a value readout and the default marked; ←/→ adjust (hold accelerates), □ resets the\n865\t  row, △ **Reset all to defaults**; mouse drags. Rows: gravity, adhesion, loop assist; for the current car: vtop, A0,\n866\t  brake, steer low/high, grip, drift grip, air yaw, ride, cd; surfaces: ice/dirt/sand/snow grip; boost Δv/accel/time;\n867\t  wall restitution; landing loss; camera distance/height/FOV/FOV-by-speed; medal ratios gold/silver/bronze; rival\n868\t  skill base/step; copper multiplier. Values live in `CFG` (session-only unless \"Keep tuning\" is on, then\n869\t  `E.store('crackmania:dev')`).\n870\t- **INFO:** car state (speed, grounded, surface, block, κ, slip, air time, boost), run (steps, CPs, respawns), track\n871\t  (id, blocks, author time, medal times), build version (`E.versionLabel()`), backend (`E.World3D.backend`).\n872\t\n873\t### 5.11 Attract mode (`attract/attract.js`)\n874\t\n875\tOn the **title and every front-end menu screen** (not the editor, garage, settings or pause), 10 s without any input\n876\t(keys, mouse movement/clicks, pad buttons or stick past the dead zone) starts the attract loop; **any input** returns to\n877\tthe title (the input is consumed). A \"DEMO — PRESS ANY BUTTON\" banner pulses at the bottom; the CRACKMANIA logo sits\n878\tsmall in a corner. Segments (each with a caption card; ~100 s total, then loops):\n879\t1. **Race** — D5 \"The Big Crack\", bot with cheats, chase cam with TV-cam cuts at the loops and the canyon jump (25 s).\n880\t2. **Build** — a time-lapse of R1 being built: blocks drop in one by one with the bounce tween, the camera orbits,\n881\t   coppers tick down; then a 3-second test drive (15 s).\n882\t3. **Puzzle** — PS1 \"Icy Connect\": missing pieces fly into place, VALIDATE, a gold medal drops (15 s).\n883\t4. **Survival** — round on R2 vs the Ghost Guild; standings card with Tex's quip (20 s).\n884\t5. **Split screen** — two bots on S2, `rows` layout (15 s).\n885\t6. **Garage** — the three cars spin through paint jobs; the medal case (10 s).\n886\tThe bots may cheat freely (lane snap, perfect grip, instant respawn). Attract also runs on touch-only devices (§5.12).\n887\t\n888\t### 5.12 Touch-only devices and the About screen\n889\t\n890\t- **Touch-only gate** (`matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')` true, `(any-pointer: fine)` false, no gamepad connected, no\n891\t  key pressed yet): the title shows the logo, a large **\"Controller or keyboard required\"** and a **SETTINGS** button\n892\t  (tap → `game.menu('settings')`). No touch controls anywhere (scenes declare `touch: []`; hide the engine's touch\n893\t  buttons). Attract mode runs after 10 s; a tap returns to the gate. A `gamepadconnected` event or any key press\n894\t  leaves the gate for the normal title.\n895\t- **About / Credits** (main menu → About): pages with large text: CRACKMANIA + version; **Source Information** (every\n896\t  field of TASK.md's list, filled from a `data/about.js` table the builder completes at the end — \"unknown\" where not\n897\t  confirmable); **Testing Feedback**, **Engine Feedback**, **Prompt Feedback** (the builder's answers, same as in the\n898\t  final reply and `exit-interview.json`); **Credits**: built on my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (MIT), three.js r182 (MIT), Rapier\n899\t  0.19.3 (Apache-2.0), AI Hub session client 1.4.0; any CC0 asset sets used (Kenney, KayKit); \"Inspired by TrackMania\n900\t  (2003) by Nadeo. CRACKMANIA is an original homage and is not affiliated with Nadeo or Ubisoft.\" The ending's credits\n901\t  roll reuses these pages with music.\n902\t\n903\t\n904\t### 5.13 Settings (the engine's screens, plus ours)\n905\t\n906\tThe engine's standard Settings and Controls screens are used as they are (no settings UI of our own): Display (full\n907\tscreen, pixel scaling, screen filter, frame rate), Sound (volume, music, effects, audio offset), Comfort (reduce\n908\tmotion, shake, flashes), Controls (rebinding per device, dead zone, vibration), plus `E.World3D.SETTINGS` (3D picture\n909\tPixels/Balanced/Full, shadows, filter; \"Characters\" cards/puppets for the crowd and hosts). Ours, via\n910\t`menu.settings` (group **Game**): **Button symbols** PlayStation / Xbox (E5), **Speed units** km/h / mph, **Default\n911\tcamera** Far / Close / Hood, **My ghost** on / off, **Coco's ghost** off / on, **Loop assist** on / off, **Steering\n912\tsensitivity** 0.5–1.5 (slider), **Hints** on / off (first-time tips). Subtitles are always on (voices are gibberish).\n913\t\n914\t---\n915\t\n916\t## 6. Content\n917\t\n918\t### 6.1 The turtle format (how the shipped tracks are written)\n919\t\n920\tA track program is a start cell, a heading and a space-separated token list (`track/turtle.js` compiles it into\n921\tplacements; the editor's own format is the placement list, and both serialize the same way). The turtle stands in the\n922\tcell it will fill next, at level L (start 0), heading h.\n923\t\n924\t| Token | Places | Then |\n925\t| --- | --- | --- |\n926\t| `ST`, `CP`, `FN`, `BO`, `BU`, `KI` | that block in the current cell (KI also reserves L+1) | move 1 cell |\n927\t| `S`, `Sn`, `DS`, `DSn`, `IS`, `ISn` | n straights (road / dirt / ice) | move n cells |\n928\t| `L1 R1 L2 R2 L3 R3`, `DL1 DR1 DL2 DR2`, `IL1 IR1 IL2 IR2`, `BL2 BR2` | the turn whose entry is the current cell (size n fills n×n) | to `c0 + (n−1)h + n·side`, heading = side |\n929\t| `U1 D1 U2 D2` | hill over 1 or 2 cells, spanning levels L..L+1 (U) or L−1..L (D) | move 1 or 2 cells, L ±1 |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66d97bf5-dd15-40b7-85f8-8eecadfc963f","uuid":"417823bb-c462-4211-b1e0-30c9e9361afc","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:03:33.125Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-050308__x1f94fb/work/PLAN.md","content":"- Coco's ghost (author run) is not stored: regenerate it by running the bot (deterministic, ~0.2 s) when needed.\n\n### 4.8 The autopilot (`race/bot.js`) — used by tests, medal baking, Survival rivals, attract mode, Dev Mode\n\n1. **Route:** walk links from Start's exit port to Finish, following each block's path in the traversed direction\n   and jump links over gaps; crossings go straight through. Sample every 2 m: `{ p, t, u, r, halfWidth (road/2 −\n   1.2 m), surface, flags: kicker|landing|loop|boost|gate, block }`. A route that doesn't reach Finish is an editor\n   error (\"Route broken at ...\").\n2. **Racing line:** lateral offsets e_i ∈ [−hw, +hw], start at 0, 80 iterations of curvature smoothing with clamping\n   (`e_i ← clamp(e_i + 0.5·((e_{i−1} + e_{i+1})/2 − e_i) − 0.3·κ_i·hw, −hw, hw)`, κ signed in the surface plane); force\n   e = 0 on loops, kickers, landings, gates and boost pads (the line goes through pads).\n3. **Speed profile:** `vmax_i = min(vtop·1.3, sqrt(a_lat / |κ_i|))`, a_lat = skillGrip·grip·surfaceGrip (+ g·sin(bank)\n   on banks); full speed through loops and kickers; then a backward pass with braking B·skillBrake and a forward pass\n   with the car's acceleration curve. Flag tracks where the speed before a kicker is below what its gap needs\n   (`v ≥ sqrt(g·gapLength/sin(30°))`·1.1) — a test fails on that.\n4. **Control (each step):** nearest route index (search a ±15-sample window after the last one, by 3D distance — never\n   jump between a loop's two lanes); lookahead point at `6 m + 0.35 s·|v|`; α = angle to it in the car's (f, r)\n   plane; `steer = clamp(1.6·α/δmax(v))`; `gas = 1` if v < target − 0.5 m/s; `brake = clamp((v − target)/5)` if\n   v > target + 1 m/s; in the air: steer 0, gas 1.\n5. **Recovery:** off the route by more than hw + 3 m for 0.6 s, slower than 1 m/s for 1.5 s after GO, or two flops in\n   a row → respawn.\n6. **Skill 0..1:** grip use 0.75 + 0.25·skill, brake margin ×(1.25 − 0.25·skill), lookahead jitter ±0.4 m·(1 −\n   skill) from `E.rng(seed)`, a lazy line (e scaled by 0.6 + 0.4·skill). Skill 1, no cheats = the **author** driver.\n7. **Cheats (attract/demo only):** lane snap (pull p toward the line, 4 m/s max), +10% grip, auto-respawn instantly.\n\n### 4.9 Medals (`race/medals.js`, `tools/bake.mjs`)\n\n- Author time = the bot at skill 1 without cheats (campaign and puzzle reference solutions), baked by\n  `node tools/bake.mjs` into `src/data/medals.json` (`{ id: { author, gold, silver, bronze } }` in steps). Re-bake\n  after any tuning change (Dev Mode has \"Re-bake this track\" for live tuning; tests fail if a baked value no longer\n  matches a fresh bot run within 1 step).\n- **Gold = author × 1.06 rounded up to 0.1 s; Silver = × 1.2 rounded up to 1 s; Bronze = × 1.5 rounded up to 1 s**\n  (TrackMania's ratios). Multipliers are Dev sliders; a track may carry `medalScale` to adjust.\n- Editor tracks: author = your validation time; the same ratios.\n- Medal icons carry letters (B, S, G, A). The Author medal is \"Coco's Time\".\n\n---\n\n## 5. Modes and features\n\n### 5.1 Profile, progression and the coppers economy (`save/profile.js`, `modes/campaign.js`)\n\nProfile (one per browser; `E.store` key `crackmania:profile`, `version: 1`, with a `migrate()` hook): name (letter\nwheel), coppers, per-track records `{ bestSteps, bestSplits, medal: 0..4, ghost, attempts }`, puzzle records, survival\nbest rank per gauntlet, unlocked packs and patterns, garage paint per car, 6 custom track slots, 10 replay slots, seen\nstory beats, first-time tips seen. In AI Hub sessions the hub gives the page empty, temporary storage: nothing to do.\n\n**Coppers (¢).** Start with **300 ¢**. Rewards are paid **once per medal tier** (earning Gold first time pays Bronze +\nSilver + Gold):\n\n| | Bronze | Silver | Gold | Author |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Race (× env: Dustbowl 1, Hedgerow 1.25, Frostpeak 1.5) | 60 | 90 | 150 | 300 |\n| Puzzle | 80 | 120 | 200 | 300 |\n\nSurvival: 50 ¢ per round survived beyond your previous best for that gauntlet, plus 300 ¢ the first time a gauntlet is\ncleared. Dev slider: copper multiplier.\n\n**Spending.** Editor blocks cost coppers when placed (refunded 100% when removed; table §4.1). Editor **packs** unlock\nfamilies of blocks: BASIC (start, finish, checkpoint, straights, turns, hills, crossing) free; STUNTS (kicker, landing,\nboost, bumps) 250 ¢; LOOPS & BANKS 600 ¢; SURFACES (dirt and ice variants) 200 ¢; SCENERY 150 ¢. Garage patterns:\n3 free, the other 5 at 100 ¢ each. Prices show on every tile; \"Not enough coppers\" plays the error buzz and shakes the\nwallet.\n\n**Unlocks.**\n- Dustbowl D1 and D2 open at start; each next track opens when the previous one has any medal.\n- An environment's **Puzzles** open when its 2nd race has a medal; its **Survival** when its 3rd race has a medal.\n- **Hedgerow** opens with medals on 3 Dustbowl races; **Frostpeak** with medals on 3 Hedgerow races.\n- Build, Hot Seat, Split Screen, Garage and Replays are open from the start (MP modes offer every track of unlocked\n  environments plus custom tracks).\n- Story beats fire on these events (§8.2). Golds on all 15 race tracks trigger the ending and the credits roll.\n\n### 5.2 Race (campaign)\n\nFront end: **Environment select** (three big cards with the car, the env emblem, medal count `G 3/5`, a lock with the\nrequirement) → **Track select** (5 tiles: number, name, a baked minimap of the route, best time, medal icon, lock;\n△ toggles \"race Coco's ghost\") → run (§4.6) → **Results** (time big; best and delta; medal drop-in with sting; next\nmedal target \"SILVER 0:31\"; coppers count-up; buttons **Retry** (△ / R), **Next track** (✕ / Enter), **Replay** (□ /\nV), **Save replay**, **Menu** (○ / Esc)). Pause menu items in races: Resume, Restart, Respawn, Camera, Ghosts,\n**Dev Mode**, Settings, Controls, Quit to menu (`menu.items` may be a function; check the engine's `v(...)` wrapper\nand return per-scene items).\n\nHUD (`ui/hud.js`, per viewport): top centre timer `0:23.41` (big digits); under it, for 2 s after a CP, the split and\ndelta; top left `CP 1/3` with a flag icon and the respawn count if > 0; top right the next medal target with its icon\n(and \"BEST 0:31.20\" under it); bottom right speed (big digits + `KM/H`, or MPH by setting) and a boost flame icon while\nboosting; centre: countdown digits (3 → 2 → 1 → GO!, scale 6, pop tween), \"MISSING CHECKPOINT\", \"FINISH!\", \"NEW\nRECORD!\". Bottom centre after a flop or when stopped for 2 s: prompt `○ Respawn  △ Restart`. Edge vignette + speed\nlines above 200 km/h (reduce-motion: off).\n\n### 5.3 Puzzle (`modes/puzzle.js`; runs inside the editor scene)\n\nA puzzle = environment, **fixed blocks** (start, checkpoints, finish; sometimes more), a **build zone** (rectangle of\ncells and levels), **no-build cells** (chasms, hedges, rocks, a pond — drawn as such), an **inventory** (block type →\ncount) and a reference solution (for its author time and for tests). The editor runs in puzzle mode: the palette shows\nonly inventory blocks with remaining counts (`R2 ×1`), fixed blocks show a lock and can't be moved, placement outside\nthe zone is refused, no coppers are spent. **Validate** = drive from start through all CPs to finish; medals by time\nagainst the solution's baked thresholds. Several routes are possible; the inventory includes extra pieces so a smarter\nroute (a boost, a wider bend) beats the obvious one. First-time Coco tip explains it in three lines.\n\n### 5.4 Build — the track editor (`editor/editor.js`)\n\nOpening: environment and slot select (6 slots with names, env emblem, validated mark and author time) → the editor.\n\nScreen: the 3D track with an **orbit camera** around the cursor; a translucent **grid** at the cursor's level (pen\nbars every cell within 6 cells of the cursor, brighter on the cursor's row/column); the **cursor** (a pulsing cell\noutline + a ghost preview of the selected block, green if it fits, red if it collides / is outside the grid / you\ncan't afford it; small arrows on its ports, blue when they'd link); placed blocks' open ports show red arrows. Top\nbar: track name, env, coppers (or puzzle counts), status chips `START ✓ FINISH ✓ CP 2 ROUTE ✓ VALIDATED 0:41.20`.\nBottom: the **palette** carousel (categories ROADS / TURNS / HILLS / STUNTS / SURFACES / SCENERY as tabs; 48×36 px\nicons baked top-down from each block's geometry; name, cost, lock if the pack isn't owned). Left: a short prompt list.\n\n| Action | DualSense | Keyboard / mouse |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| move cursor (camera-relative, repeats) | left stick | WASD / arrows; mouse hover picks the cell under the pointer on the cursor's level (ray–plane) |\n| palette item / category | d-pad ←/→ / ↑/↓ | Tab / Shift+Tab categories, 1–9 items, mouse click on a tile |\n| place | ✕ | Space / Enter / left click |\n| remove block under cursor | □ | Delete / Backspace / right click |\n| rotate selected block | R1 (cw) / L1 (ccw) | R / Shift+R / mouse wheel |\n| level up / down | R2 / L2 | E / Q / Shift+wheel / PageUp / PageDown |\n| orbit / tilt camera | right stick | middle-drag or Alt+left-drag; wheel+Ctrl zooms |\n| test drive from Start | △ | T |\n| undo / redo | L3 / R3 | Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y |\n| editor menu | Options | Esc |\n\nEditor menu: Resume, **Validate** (a run from Start; finishing with every CP sets the author time and medals; any\nedit afterwards clears it), Test drive, Save, Save as, Load, Rename (letter wheel), Environment (only when empty),\nShare code (shows a base64url code in a large box; Copy uses `navigator.clipboard` when allowed), Import code (a text\nfield; keyboard paste), Clear track (asks), Dev Mode, Settings, Exit. Test drive returns to the same cursor and\ncamera. Undo/redo stack of 200 operations (place, remove, rotate, rename) with coppers refunded/charged.\n\nRules: one Start (free), at least one Finish (free), any number of CPs; blocks can't overlap (3D occupancy) but can\nsit above others with ≥ 1 level of clearance (supports are generated automatically and never block a lane under\nthem); gaps under kickers are reserved automatically when a kicker is placed (shown hatched). A track is shareable\nand playable in Hot Seat / Split Screen once validated. A Dev Mode button \"Export as content\" prints a `data/tracks.js`\nentry (placements + metadata) — the designer workflow for growing the game later.\n\n### 5.5 Survival (`modes/survival.js`)\n\nPer environment a **gauntlet of 5 rounds** = that environment's race tracks 1→5 (rounds may include tracks not yet\nopen in Race: Survival is their preview). Each round: you vs the **Ghost Guild** — Tex Mirage, Mlle Gravillon, Bobo\nYeti — as ghost cars with name tags. Their runs are bot runs generated at round start (behind a 1-second \"WARMING UP\nTHE GHOSTS\" card; deterministic per gauntlet + round): skills `base + 0.03·round + 0.02·rankIndex` with bases 0.78 /\n0.86 / 0.93 and different seeds (Tex jittery-fast, Gravillon clean, Bobo late braker). Place by finish time (DNF after\nthe last rival finishes + 15 s = last). **1st: +2 ranks, 2nd: +1, 3rd: stay, 4th: out.** Ranks: ROOKIE → DRIVER →\nRACER → PILOT → ACE → MANIAC → CRACKMANIAC. Between rounds: standings card with portraits and a rival quip (§8.2).\nClearing round 5 = \"GAUNTLET CLEARED\" + rewards. Best rank per gauntlet is recorded.\n\n### 5.6 Hot Seat and Split Screen (`modes/hotseat.js`, `modes/split.js`)\n\n**Hot Seat** (TrackMania 2003's local mode): 2–8 players (default names PLAYER 1…; letter wheel to rename), attempts\nper turn 1/2/3, a cup of 1–5 tracks (pick or random). Turn order rotates per track. Before each turn a full-screen\ncard \"PASS THE CONTROLLER TO {NAME}\" (Coco babbles; any button when ready). The leader's best run drives as a ghost.\nScoring per track: 10-8-6-5-4-3-2-1 by best time; cup standings after each track; a podium at the end with each\nplayer's car in their paint colour (assign 8 distinct colours).\n\n**Split Screen:** 2–4 players at once. Join screen: each pad presses ✕ or Options to join (`game.allowJoin({ max: 4 })`),\nkeyboard players join with Enter (left half: WASD + F/G/H) or Numpad Enter (right half: arrows + . / ,), per the\nengine's half-keyboard support. Layout `rows` for 2, `grid` for 3–4 (`game.splitScreen(n, { layout })`,\n`world.addCamera()` per extra viewport; filters are off while split — engine rule). Same countdown; cars are ghosts to\neach other (no collisions, TrackMania style). Each viewport has its own HUD; a player who finishes sees their place;\nthe race ends when all finish or 30 s after the first finish. Best of 1 / 3 races.\n\n### 5.7 Online — AI Hub sessions (`modes/online.js`; protocol at `ai-hub/lib/hub/README.md`)\n\nMode **`ghost`**: each player runs their own copy of the round; positions are exchanged so each copy shows the others\nas ghost cars; nothing they do affects your world. This *is* TrackMania online (cars never collide).\n\nHead metas (in the built HTML):\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"ghost\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"3\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Best time in 3 minutes wins; retry as often as you like\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"R2/W gas · L2/S brake · stick/arrows steer · Circle/Enter respawn\">\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\"><meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1-4\">\n```\nFlow when `AIHub.active` (true from the first line):\n1. Skip title, attract and menus entirely. Boot, then `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'ghost', seats: [1, 4],\n   card: true })`. If `info` is null, run the normal game.\n2. Pick the round's track with `AIHub.rng('track')` from the session list **D1, D2, D3, R1, R2, S1, S2** (the same\n   pick on every copy; the seed changes per round, so rounds rotate tracks); load it.\n3. **Own card** (§ \"The card\" in the README): the track flyover looping, the track name, each player's name in their\n   seat colour (`info.players[].color`: #e8443a, #3b82f6, #22c55e, #f5b700) with a READY tick from the `card` event's\n   `ready` ids, the goal, the controls for this player's device, and the time left (`card.left`). Enter / ✕ / a tap →\n   `AIHub.answer('ready')`; △ (button 3) or M → `AIHub.answer('more')`. The card has no menus and draws no\n   `Math.random` (use `AIHub.rng('card')` for any jitter). Call `AIHub.ready()` once the world is built — no key press.\n4. On `start`, show 3-2-1-GO against `AIHub.time()` (play begins at 0). Then **time attack**: unlimited restarts and\n   respawns; the round clock (3:00 from `AIHub.time() = 0`) shows top centre; your best time top right.\n5. Every ~100 ms send `{ t: 'g', area: trackId, run: runCounter, ms, p: [x, y, z] (rounded 0.1 unit), q: [x, y, z, w]\n   (4 decimals), v: kmh, f: flags }` with `AIHub.send(data, { reliable: false })` (≤ 10/s, well under the 20/s limit,\n   < 200 bytes). On a new best, send `{ t: 'best', ms }` reliably. Receivers buffer 150 ms and interpolate; a ghost\n   whose `area` differs is hidden; show name tags in seat colours (names drawn by the pixel font on canvas — never as\n   HTML).\n6. Each second `AIHub.progress({ score, label })`: with a best, `score = 2e6 − bestMs`, label `BEST 0:42.31`; without,\n   `score = cpsThisRun·1000 + metresAlongRoute`, label `CP 2/3`.\n7. At 3:00 by `AIHub.time()` (or 5 s before `info.limitMs` if that is sooner) — or at once on `time-up` — call `AIHub.result({ time: bestMs })` if you have a finish,\n   else `AIHub.result({ score })`, exactly once, then show \"WAITING FOR THE OTHERS\" with live ghosts. Include `stats:\n   { Runs: n, Respawns: n }`.\n8. On `end`: stop input and sound (`game.audio.mute(true)`, freeze), show the hub's standings line if given.\n9. On `leave`: remove that ghost. If WebGL 2/WebGPU init fails: `AIHub.fail('3D graphics are not available')`.\n10. In a session: no Quit to title, no title/attract/editor/garage, no `alert/confirm/prompt`, no `window.open`, no\n    network except the hub; Options is ignored while Create (Pad8) is held.\nThe Multiplayer menu outside the hub shows an **Online** tile that explains: \"Online races run in AI Hub sessions —\nopen CRACKMANIA from AI Hub with friends.\"\n\n### 5.8 Replays (`modes/replay.js`)\n\nFrom results (\"Replay\") or the Replays list (10 slots: track, time, car, date; delete with □). Viewer: the run's\nghost drawn as a normal (opaque) car with its paint, the HUD's timer and CP splits replayed, camera modes **Chase / TV\n/ Orbit** (R1 / C cycles), play/pause (✕ / Space), scrub (left stick or ←/→; hold for 4×), speed 0.25×–4× (L2/R2 or\n−/=), restart (△ / Home), exit (○ / Esc), mouse: drag to orbit, wheel to zoom, click the timeline bar to seek.\nCustom-track replays embed the track.\n\n### 5.9 Garage — paint shop (`modes/garage.js`)\n\nA small **workshop world** (a separate `E.World3D` with a text `level`: brick walls, a car lift, torches, shelves,\ncrates, barrels, a tyre rack — core shapes plus a few custom ones) with a turntable. Pick car (locked cars show a\nsilhouette and the unlock requirement), then: **Body colour**, **Accent colour** (24-swatch grids, plus HSV sliders),\n**Pattern** (Solid, Twin Stripes, Side Stripe, Checker Roof, Flames, Lightning, Number Panel, Two-Tone), **Pattern\ncolour**, **Number** (00–99, drawn on doors and roof with a 3×5 pixel digit font made of thin boxes), **Rims**\n(6 colours), **Helmet colour**. Live preview spins; △ toggles \"lights on\". Saved per car; used in every mode, replays,\nhub ghosts (others see their seat colour, you see your paint).\n\n### 5.10 Dev Mode (`ui/dev.js`; pause menu → \"Dev Mode\")\n\nAn overlay panel (left 45% of the screen, game visible and paused, or running in slow motion if chosen) with three\ntabs (L1/R1, Q/E, click):\n- **TOOLS:** Teleport to next / previous checkpoint; Finish now (records the current time); Award medal (B/S/G/A);\n  Unlock everything; +1000 coppers; Reset profile (asks); Bot drives (toggle, skill slider); Re-bake medals for this\n  track; Time scale 0.25× / 0.5× / 1×; Frame step (while paused); Free camera (fly with sticks/WASD); Show probes\n  (wheel rays, contact plane, normal, κ, slip); Show colliders (wireframe of collision triangles, pen bars); Show route\n  and racing line; Show gates; Show FPS and draw stats (`renderer.info`); Jump to (any track / puzzle / gauntlet\n  round / scene by deep link).\n- **TUNING:** live sliders with a value readout and the default marked; ←/→ adjust (hold accelerates), □ resets the\n  row, △ **Reset all to defaults**; mouse drags. Rows: gravity, adhesion, loop assist; for the current car: vtop, A0,\n  brake, steer low/high, grip, drift grip, air yaw, ride, cd; surfaces: ice/dirt/sand/snow grip; boost Δv/accel/time;\n  wall restitution; landing loss; camera distance/height/FOV/FOV-by-speed; medal ratios gold/silver/bronze; rival\n  skill base/step; copper multiplier. Values live in `CFG` (session-only unless \"Keep tuning\" is on, then\n  `E.store('crackmania:dev')`).\n- **INFO:** car state (speed, grounded, surface, block, κ, slip, air time, boost), run (steps, CPs, respawns), track\n  (id, blocks, author time, medal times), build version (`E.versionLabel()`), backend (`E.World3D.backend`).\n\n### 5.11 Attract mode (`attract/attract.js`)\n\nOn the **title and every front-end menu screen** (not the editor, garage, settings or pause), 10 s without any input\n(keys, mouse movement/clicks, pad buttons or stick past the dead zone) starts the attract loop; **any input** returns to\nthe title (the input is consumed). A \"DEMO — PRESS ANY BUTTON\" banner pulses at the bottom; the CRACKMANIA logo sits\nsmall in a corner. Segments (each with a caption card; ~100 s total, then loops):\n1. **Race** — D5 \"The Big Crack\", bot with cheats, chase cam with TV-cam cuts at the loops and the canyon jump (25 s).\n2. **Build** — a time-lapse of R1 being built: blocks drop in one by one with the bounce tween, the camera orbits,\n   coppers tick down; then a 3-second test drive (15 s).\n3. **Puzzle** — PS1 \"Icy Connect\": missing pieces fly into place, VALIDATE, a gold medal drops (15 s).\n4. **Survival** — round on R2 vs the Ghost Guild; standings card with Tex's quip (20 s).\n5. **Split screen** — two bots on S2, `rows` layout (15 s).\n6. **Garage** — the three cars spin through paint jobs; the medal case (10 s).\nThe bots may cheat freely (lane snap, perfect grip, instant respawn). Attract also runs on touch-only devices (§5.12).\n\n### 5.12 Touch-only devices and the About screen\n\n- **Touch-only gate** (`matchMedia('(pointer: coarse)')` true, `(any-pointer: fine)` false, no gamepad connected, no\n  key pressed yet): the title shows the logo, a large **\"Controller or keyboard required\"** and a **SETTINGS** button\n  (tap → `game.menu('settings')`). No touch controls anywhere (scenes declare `touch: []`; hide the engine's touch\n  buttons). Attract mode runs after 10 s; a tap returns to the gate. A `gamepadconnected` event or any key press\n  leaves the gate for the normal title.\n- **About / Credits** (main menu → About): pages with large text: CRACKMANIA + version; **Source Information** (every\n  field of TASK.md's list, filled from a `data/about.js` table the builder completes at the end — \"unknown\" where not\n  confirmable); **Testing Feedback**, **Engine Feedback**, **Prompt Feedback** (the builder's answers, same as in the\n  final reply and `exit-interview.json`); **Credits**: built on my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (MIT), three.js r182 (MIT), Rapier\n  0.19.3 (Apache-2.0), AI Hub session client 1.4.0; any CC0 asset sets used (Kenney, KayKit); \"Inspired by TrackMania\n  (2003) by Nadeo. CRACKMANIA is an original homage and is not affiliated with Nadeo or Ubisoft.\" The ending's credits\n  roll reuses these pages with music.\n\n\n### 5.13 Settings (the engine's screens, plus ours)\n\nThe engine's standard Settings and Controls screens are used as they are (no settings UI of our own): Display (full\nscreen, pixel scaling, screen filter, frame rate), Sound (volume, music, effects, audio offset), Comfort (reduce\nmotion, shake, flashes), Controls (rebinding per device, dead zone, vibration), plus `E.World3D.SETTINGS` (3D picture\nPixels/Balanced/Full, shadows, filter; \"Characters\" cards/puppets for the crowd and hosts). Ours, via\n`menu.settings` (group **Game**): **Button symbols** PlayStation / Xbox (E5), **Speed units** km/h / mph, **Default\ncamera** Far / Close / Hood, **My ghost** on / off, **Coco's ghost** off / on, **Loop assist** on / off, **Steering\nsensitivity** 0.5–1.5 (slider), **Hints** on / off (first-time tips). Subtitles are always on (voices are gibberish).\n\n---\n\n## 6. Content\n\n### 6.1 The turtle format (how the shipped tracks are written)\n\nA track program is a start cell, a heading and a space-separated token list (`track/turtle.js` compiles it into\nplacements; the editor's own format is the placement list, and both serialize the same way). The turtle stands in the\ncell it will fill next, at level L (start 0), heading h.\n\n| Token | Places | Then |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `ST`, `CP`, `FN`, `BO`, `BU`, `KI` | that block in the current cell (KI also reserves L+1) | move 1 cell |\n| `S`, `Sn`, `DS`, `DSn`, `IS`, `ISn` | n straights (road / dirt / ice) | move n cells |\n| `L1 R1 L2 R2 L3 R3`, `DL1 DR1 DL2 DR2`, `IL1 IR1 IL2 IR2`, `BL2 BR2` | the turn whose entry is the current cell (size n fills n×n) | to `c0 + (n−1)h + n·side`, heading = side |\n| `U1 D1 U2 D2` | hill over 1 or 2 cells, spanning levels L..L+1 (U) or L−1..L (D) | move 1 or 2 cells, L ±1 |","numLines":300,"startLine":630,"totalLines":1464}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011besEUKboWSCdmPoLzp18e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
