{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018t2i22iq3Hr3KunW4QpAcX","type":"tool_result","content":"1229\t// tools/node-env.mjs — the engine, the 3D engine and the game in Node, no browser\n1230\timport { registerHooks } from 'node:module';\n1231\timport { pathToFileURL, fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\n1232\timport vm from 'node:vm';\n1233\timport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n1234\tconst ROOT = fileURLToPath(new URL('..', import.meta.url)), V = ROOT + 'engine/vendor/';\n1235\tconst MAP = { 'three': 'three-0.182.0/three.webgpu.min.js', 'three/webgpu': 'three-0.182.0/three.webgpu.min.js',\n1236\t  'three/tsl': 'three-0.182.0/three.tsl.min.js', '@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat': 'rapier3d-simd-compat-0.19.3/rapier.js' };\n1237\tregisterHooks({ resolve: (spec, ctx, next) => MAP[spec] ? { url: pathToFileURL(V + MAP[spec]).href, format: 'module', shortCircuit: true } : next(spec, ctx) });\n1238\tvm.runInThisContext(readFileSync(ROOT + 'engine/my-3d2dge.js', 'utf8'), { filename: 'my-3d2dge.js' });  // globalThis.My3D2dge\n1239\texport const E = globalThis.My3D2dge;\n1240\t// World3D bakes textures on canvases: hand it the 2D engine's headless stand-in canvas\n1241\tconst standIn = () => { const d = globalThis.document; delete globalThis.document; const c = E.mkCanvas(1, 1); globalThis.document = d; return c; };\n1242\tglobalThis.document = { createElement: standIn, getElementById: () => null, querySelector: () => null, addEventListener() {}, removeEventListener() {} };\n1243\tawait import(pathToFileURL(ROOT + 'engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js').href);                                   // E.World3D, E.THREE, E.RAPIER\n1244\texport async function makeGame(o = {}) {\n1245\t  const { createGame } = await import(pathToFileURL(ROOT + 'src/main.js').href);\n1246\t  const g = await createGame({ headless: true, ...o }); await g.game.booted; return g;                 // { game, api }\n1247\t}\n1248\t```\n1249\tIn Node, `new E.Game({ headless: true })` has no screen and skips `draw`; `E.World3D.init(game)` returns after\n1250\t`RAPIER.init()` without a renderer; worlds build their meshes but never render. Rapier prints a harmless \"deprecated\n1251\tparameters\" warning on init — filter it from test output.\n1252\t\n1253\t### 9.2 The one command\n1254\t\n1255\t`node tools/test.mjs [suite ...] [--browser] [--hub] [--all]` loads the engine once, runs the suites in-process, and\n1256\tprints **only** `FAIL <suite>: <check>: <detail>` lines and one summary line (`247 checks, 0 failed, 12.4 s`); exit\n1257\tcode 1 on any failure. `--browser` adds §9.5, `--hub` adds §9.6, `--all` both. Each suite lists the source files it\n1258\tcovers (`covers: ['src/car/**', 'src/track/**']`) so you rerun only what a change touches. Use `game.advance(s)`,\n1259\t`input.hold/tap/press`, `game.debug.snapshot()` and the `api` handle (load track, place car, run bot, editor\n1260\toperations, fake AI Hub) — the engine's `game/test.mjs` pattern.\n1261\t\n1262\t`game.debug.snapshot()` returns at least: `{ scene, page, mode, env, track, run: { phase, steps, cps, cpTotal,\n1263\trespawns, finished, medal }, car: { x, y, z, kmh, grounded, surface, block, up }, profile: { coppers, medals, unlocked\n1264\t}, ui: { focus, prompt }, attract, touchGate, hub: { active, phase }, errors: game.errors.length }`.\n1265\t\n1266\t### 9.3 Suites and what they check\n1267\t\n1268\t| Suite | Checks (each a named check) |\n1269\t| --- | --- |\n1270\t| `turtle` | every track and puzzle program compiles; no overlaps; in bounds; expected CP counts; kicker→landing links; puzzle fixed blocks equal the solution's ST/CP/FN cells; inventories cover the solutions |\n1271\t| `blocks` | every block type: path is C0/C1 continuous (Δp < 1 cm, Δt < 0.5° between samples), unit t/u, u ⊥ t; mesh has no NaN; Rapier winding normals agree with u (dot > 0.5) and three winding is the reverse; **every link in every shipped track**: port frames match (1 cm, 0.5°) |\n1272\t| `physics` | (Coyote unless noted) 0→100 km/h in 2.3–3.3 s; reaches ≥ 97% vtop on a long straight; 100→0 braking in 12–22 m; R2 at 90 km/h holds the lane, R2 at 130 km/h and R1 at 80 km/h run wide (they need braking); BR2 holds at 150 km/h; **loop block on full throttle from ≥ 60 km/h: grounded all the way, exits upright; from ≤ 40 km/h: detaches at the top; coasting from ≥ 115 km/h holds, ≤ 95 km/h fails** (re-measure and update these numbers if tuning changes); ice: acceleration capped by traction (≤ 0.35 × asphalt's from standstill); U1 crest at 120 km/h: airborne; kicker at the D2 approach: lands on the landing; wall at 100 km/h at 30°: no penetration, speed kept 40–90%; ice cornering speed < 70% of asphalt's; boost pad adds ≥ 9 m/s; flop recovers upright within 1 s; respawn → at the CP, v = 0, upright; 10 s of identical inputs twice → identical state hash |\n1273\t| `race` | CPs count once each, in any order, either direction; finish refused before all CPs (\"MISSING CHECKPOINT\"); clock runs through respawns; restart resets; splits and deltas vs best; medal thresholds from author (1.06/1.2/1.5 with rounding); results rewards paid once per tier; records saved |\n1274\t| `ghost` | a recorded bot run plays back within 2 cm / 1° of the live car at every sample; encode/decode round trip exact; size < 25 KB/min |\n1275\t| `bot` | skill 1 finishes all 15 tracks and 6 puzzle solutions with 0 respawns; steps equal `medals.json` (±1); skill 0.8 finishes slower; speed plan reaches every gap's required speed |\n1276\t| `campaign` | unlock rules (D1–D2 open; next on medal; puzzles/survival/env gates); coppers ledger (rewards, block costs, refunds, packs, patterns); story beats fire once; profile save/load/migrate |\n1277\t| `editor` | place/rotate/raise/remove with occupancy and costs; refuse overlaps, out-of-grid, unaffordable; kicker reserves its gap; undo/redo 50 random ops returns to the same state and coppers; validate (bot drive) sets author + medals; any edit clears validation; save/load slots; share code round trip; export-as-content output compiles |\n1278\t| `puzzle` | fixed blocks locked; inventory counts enforced; zone and no-build cells enforced; each reference solution placed through the editor API validates and earns at least Gold at skill 1 |\n1279\t| `survival` | rival runs deterministic per gauntlet+round; placing rules (+2/+1/0/out); rank names; elimination ends the run; clearing pays once |\n1280\t| `hotseat` | 3 players × 2 attempts × 2 tracks with scripted bot turns → correct standings and points; pass-the-controller cards between turns |\n1281\t| `split` | 2 and 4 players: viewports and cameras created and removed; each car finishes; HUD per viewport; no car–car collisions |\n1282\t| `online` | with a **fake AIHub** object (connect → info, card events, start, time, send/receive, time-up, end, leave): no title/menus; `ready()` once without input; Enter answers ready on our card; ghost messages ≤ 10/s and < 1 KB; progress each second; exactly one `result`; input and sound stop on `end`; outside a session nothing changes |\n1283\t| `ui` | title → menu → every page reachable by keys only and by simulated mouse clicks (`input.feed`), and back; focus never lost; prompt glyphs switch keyboard ↔ gamepad (PlayStation) ↔ Xbox setting; Dev Mode opens from the pause menu, a slider changes `CFG` live, Reset restores defaults; attract starts after 10 s idle on title and on the main menu, not in the editor; any input exits; touch-only flag shows the gate with Settings |\n1284\t| `playthrough` | **the whole game, scripted**: fresh profile → welcome beat → all 15 races driven by the bot as the player through the real menus (pressing the real buttons) → medals, coppers and unlocks as designed → the 6 puzzles solved through the editor UI → each gauntlet run (bot at skill 1 clears it) → build and validate a 12-block track in the editor, save, reload, share code → paint a car in the garage → save and reopen a replay → hot seat (2 players) and split screen (2 players) races → golds everywhere → ending beat and credits → final profile matches expectations; 0 engine errors |\n1285\t\n1286\t### 9.4 Rules for testing\n1287\t\n1288\t- Keep checks state-based (snapshot fields, profile values, physics numbers). Use screenshots only for looks.\n1289\t- Rerun a suite only after changing code it covers; run `--all` before each milestone exit and at the end.\n1290\t- Don't use subagents or workflows to review, judge or audit (TASK.md). Fix the first failure first.\n1291\t\n1292\t### 9.5 Browser checks (`tools/browser.mjs`, Playwright 1.63 + Chromium; built HTML opened from `file://`)\n1293\t\n1294\tLaunch Chromium with `--use-angle=swiftshader --enable-unsafe-swiftshader --ignore-gpu-blocklist\n1295\t--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required`. Checks: no page errors or console errors; boot finishes within 60 s;\n1296\t`window.__crack.snapshot().scene === 'title'`; the canvas is not blank (pixel variance); `?backend=webgl` also boots;\n1297\tdeep links `#race/D3`, `#race/R3`, `#race/S3`, `#editor`, `#puzzle/PD2`, `#survival/hedgerow`, `#split/2/S2`,\n1298\t`#garage`, `#replay/last`, `#about`, `#lab/physics`, `#lab/blocks` each reach their scene; the bot's D1 and D3 times in\n1299\tthe browser equal `medals.json` (determinism Node ↔ browser); attract starts after 10 s idle and a key press ends it;\n1300\ta touch-only context (`hasTouch: true, isMobile: true`, 390×844) shows the gate text and the Settings button and runs\n1301\tattract. Screenshots to `check-output/` for review: title, each environment at a signature spot (D3 loop, D5 canyon\n1302\tjump mid-air, R3 crossing, S3 drop, Frostpeak lamps), HUD at a CP split, results with a medal, editor with palette,\n1303\tpuzzle zone, survival standings, split screen ×4, garage, replay TV cam, Dev Mode, About. The engine's\n1304\t`tools/check.mjs` also works on the built file (`node engine/tools/check.mjs <file>#race/D3`) — act on its look notes.\n1305\t\n1306\t### 9.6 AI Hub harness (`tools/hub.mjs`)\n1307\t\n1308\tCopy `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` and the built HTML (as `game.html`) into `<devfolder>/.hubtest/`;\n1309\tstart `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory .hubtest`, read the port it prints, fetch `game.html`\n1310\tand confirm its `<title>` is CRACKMANIA (it's ours, not another agent's server); then in Playwright open\n1311\t`harness.html?game=game.html&players=2&auto=1&limit=45`, wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, require\n1312\t`window.__hubCheck.pass === true`; repeat with `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&limit=45` and with\n1313\t`&scenario=host-leave`. Print failing checks' names and details. Stop the server by its PID. (The round respects\n1314\t`info.limitMs`: end the time attack 5 s before it when shorter than 3 minutes.)\n1315\t\n1316\t---\n1317\t\n1318\t## 10. Build order and milestones\n1319\t\n1320\tEach milestone ends with its exit checks green (`node tools/test.mjs <its suites>`), a build, and a short look in the\n1321\tbrowser. Do them in order — later ones lean on earlier ones (the bot in M3 is what tests everything after it).\n1322\t\n1323\t| M | Scope | Exit |\n1324\t| --- | --- | --- |\n1325\t| **M0 Foundations** (de-risk first) | dev folder, engine copy (§2.2), engine changes E1–E6, `package.json`, `node-env.mjs`, `test.mjs` skeleton, `build.mjs`; a Dustbowl world (terrain, sky, sun, fog), one straight block mesh, a pen box car, HUD text | headless boot test green; the built single HTML opens from `file://` in headless Chromium with no errors and a non-blank 3D picture under the HUD |\n1326\t| **M1 Drive** | blocks ST/FN/CP/S/turns/hills; ribbon mesher, cross-sections, base plate, boundary, colliders; CarSim complete (§4.4); far/close/hood cameras; Coyote model; minimal HUD | `physics` (flat, turns, crest, walls, determinism), `blocks` for those types; D1 drivable |\n1327\t| **M2 Stunts + catalogue** | kicker/gap/landing/chasm, loop + lane assist, boost, banked, crossing, bumps, dirt/ice/snow, supports, rails; turtle compiler; all 15 tracks; `#lab/blocks`, `#lab/physics` | `turtle`, `blocks`, loop/jump `physics` checks; screenshots of every track |\n1328\t| **M3 Racing** | run rules, gates, respawn/restart, splits, basic results; ghosts; bot; `bake.mjs`; `medals.json` | `race`, `ghost`, `bot` |\n1329\t| **M4 Worlds and art** | three environments (terrain, sky, plate textures, palettes), Pebble and Moose, paint system, deco + trackside dressing, new shapes, animated props, FX, Drapeau, crowd, gates' boards and lights | screenshots reviewed (§9.5 list); check.mjs look notes handled |\n1330\t| **M5 Sound** | car synth, SFX, songs, stings, babble | headless no-op verified; manual listen in browser; mute/volume honoured |\n1331\t| **M6 Front end + campaign** | UI kit, glyphs, prompt bar, title, menus, env/track select, results, profile, unlocks, coppers, story beats, tips, settings, per-scene pause items | `ui` (minus attract/dev), `campaign` |\n1332\t| **M7 Editor + Puzzle** | editor scene, controls, palette, packs, undo/redo, test drive, validate, slots, codes, export; puzzle mode; 6 puzzles | `editor`, `puzzle` |\n1333\t| **M8 Modes** | Survival, Hot Seat, Split Screen, Replays, Garage | `survival`, `hotseat`, `split`, replay/garage checks in `ui` |\n1334\t| **M9 Online** | AI Hub ghost mode, own card | `online`; `--hub` all three runs pass |\n1335\t| **M10 Shell features** | Dev Mode, attract mode, touch gate, About/Credits, ending + credits roll | full `ui`; `--browser` |\n1336\t| **M11 Finish** | `playthrough`; balance pass with Dev sliders (re-bake medals); polish; final build; About texts; `exit-interview.json`; final reply | `node tools/test.mjs --all` green; deliverables in place (§12) |\n1337\t\n1338\t---\n1339\t\n1340\t## 11. Risks and how to de-risk them\n1341\t\n1342\t| Risk | Mitigation |\n1343\t| --- | --- |\n1344\t| Car physics through loops/jumps feels wrong or is unstable | Build exactly the validated model (§4.4, Appendix A); keep the four-point plane fit, the curvature filter and the 0.06 s detach grace; lane assist on loops; physics tests encode the intended behaviour (fast holds, slow falls); `#lab/physics` and live sliders for tuning; re-bake medals after tuning |\n1345\t| Bundling three + Rapier + the ESM 3D engine into one file that runs from `file://` | Prove it in M0 before anything else; esbuild plugin resolution; escape `</script`; fallback import map to jsDelivr (allowed) |\n1346\t| Headless testing of a 3D engine | The loader in §9.1 was run successfully during planning; keep pure logic (track model, CarSim, run, bot, economy, editor ops) free of three.js calls so most suites don't depend on rendering at all |\n1347\t| Block seams (cracks, bumps, wrong normals at joints) | Shared exact port frames; per-link tests; ribbons sample the exact end points; `#lab/blocks` shows every block in a row |\n1348\t| Bot can't drive some track (bake, Survival, attract and tests all depend on it) | Route window search (no lane jumping in loops), recovery rules, speed plan that knows gaps; the `bot` suite over all content; skill 1 must finish with 0 respawns — if not, fix the track (add a boost, widen a bend) rather than the bot |\n1349\t| Node vs browser determinism of baked times | No wall-clock or renderer reads in simulation; same V8 + same Rapier WASM; browser check compares D1/D3 times |\n1350\t| Editor is clumsy on a pad at 10 feet | Build cursor + palette first in M7 and try: a 10-block track with only the pad in under 2 minutes; mouse parity (hover picks cells); big icons; red/green preview |\n1351\t| AI Hub conformance | All session code in `modes/online.js`; fake-hub unit suite; the real harness in three configurations; README rules as a checklist |\n1352\t| Shader stalls on track load / editing | All materials and pen batches (incl. ghost) made at boot; `world.prepare()`; only geometry changes later; dispose old geometries |\n1353\t| WebGPU vs WebGL 2 | three falls back by itself; test `?backend=webgl`; never read back from the GPU (engine rule) |\n1354\t| Scope | Build each feature's minimal complete form end to end first (e.g. garage with colours and 3 patterns), then deepen; nothing ships half-done |\n1355\t| Shared machine, full `/tmp` | Caches and temp files inside the dev folder; only your own PIDs; servers on 127.0.0.1 with an OS port |\n1356\t\n1357\t---\n1358\t\n1359\t## 12. Finishing: deliverables, About, exit interview, final reply\n1360\t\n1361\t- `Crackmania-TrackMania2003-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174810.html` in the root (beside TASK.md), built by\n1362\t  `node tools/build.mjs` from a clean checkout of the dev folder; opens from `file://` with no errors; passes the hub\n1363\t  harness; title screen reads **CRACKMANIA**.\n1364\t- The dev folder holds everything needed to rebuild and retest (`npm install`, `node tools/test.mjs --all`,\n1365\t  `node tools/build.mjs`); `engine/CHANGES.md` lists E1–E6 and anything else changed, with the reason.\n1366\t- About/Credits pages and the final chat reply carry the same **Source Information** (Date `2026-11-03 17:48:10`;\n1367\t  Source `TrackMania (2003, Nadeo)`; Plan `PLAN.md`; Genre and Perspective `Arcade racing (time attack) and\n1368\t  track-building puzzle; third-person chase camera, orbiting editor camera`; Tech `my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (2D engine + 3D\n1369\t  engine), three.js r182 (WebGPU/WebGL 2), Rapier 0.19.3, esbuild (build), Playwright 1.63 (tests)`; Art Direction\n1370\t  `the engine's native low-res toon 3D with ink outlines and code-drawn pixel textures`; Animation `engine rigs, poses,\n1371\t  tweens and scripts plus code-driven car/prop animation`; Audio `engine chip synth songs, WebAudio car synth, Animalese-\n1372\t  style gibberish voices`; Online `AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode`; Testing `headless Node suites with\n1373\t  game.advance/game.debug, a scripted whole-game playthrough, Playwright checks of the built file, the AI Hub\n1374\t  harness`; Research `what you actually did`; Environment `Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown`; Model\n1375\t  `Anthropic, <your model id>, reasoning effort <yours>`; Usage `estimates or \"unknown\"`) and the answers to the\n1376\t  **Testing / Engine / Prompt Feedback** questions (TASK.md lists them).\n1377\t- `exit-interview.json` beside the HTML, in TASK.md's exact shape, every value filled, plain text, checked with\n1378\t  `node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'))\"`. Suggested `aiHub` block:\n1379\t  `name` \"CRACKMANIA\", `tagline` \"Crack the clock.\", `description` \"Block-built stunt tracks, loops and canyon jumps\n1380\t  against the clock: race, solve track puzzles, survive the Ghost Guild and build your own tracks.\", `type` \"Game\",\n1381\t  `genre` \"Racing\", `source` \"TrackMania (2003)\", `series` \"TrackMania\", `players` \"1–4\", `controls` \"R2/W gas, L2/S\n1382\t  brake, left stick/arrows steer, Circle/Enter respawn, Triangle/Delete restart\", `tags` [\"3d\", \"arcade\", \"vehicles\",\n1383\t  \"versus\", \"retro\", \"low-poly\"].\n1384\t- Final reply: a short summary of the game plus the four information blocks above.\n1385\t\n1386\t---\n1387\t\n1388\t## Appendix A — the validated car core (reference code from the planning spike)\n1389\t\n1390\tEngine units (`U = 16` per metre), z up, `dt = 1/120`. `pw` is TrackPhysics' Rapier world (fixed trimesh colliders\n1391\tonly), `RAPIER` the module (`E.RAPIER`). This exact code produced §4.4's prototype results; §4.4 adds steering, the\n1392\tgrip/drift model, surfaces, boost, walls, flop, landing loss and lane assist on top of it. Vectors are `[x, y, z]`\n1393\tarrays.\n1394\t\n1395\t```js\n1396\tconst cross = (a, b) => [a[1]*b[2]-a[2]*b[1], a[2]*b[0]-a[0]*b[2], a[0]*b[1]-a[1]*b[0]];\n1397\tconst add = (a, b, k = 1) => [a[0]+b[0]*k, a[1]+b[1]*k, a[2]+b[2]*k], dot = (a, b) => a[0]*b[0]+a[1]*b[1]+a[2]*b[2];\n1398\tconst len = a => Math.hypot(a[0], a[1], a[2]), norm = a => { const l = len(a) || 1; return [a[0]/l, a[1]/l, a[2]/l]; };\n1399\t// Coyote-like tuning in engine units (cd: 0.0004 per metre = 0.0004/U per unit)\n1400\tconst T = { ride: .55*U, reach: .9*U, A0: 12*U, vtop: 64*U, cd: .0004/U, adhesion: .35*9.81*U, align: 30, mu: 1 };\n1401\tconst WHEELS = [[1.35*U, -.8*U], [1.35*U, .8*U], [-1.35*U, -.8*U], [-1.35*U, .8*U]];   // FL, FR, RL, RR (right = +y)\n1402\tfunction probe(c) {\n1403\t  const r = cross(c.u, c.f), hits = [];\n1404\t  for (const [lx, ly] of WHEELS) {\n1405\t    const o = add(add(add(c.p, c.f, lx), r, ly), c.u, U * .5);            // from half a metre above the floor\n1406\t    const h = pw.castRayAndGetNormal(new RAPIER.Ray({ x: o[0], y: o[1], z: o[2] }, { x: -c.u[0], y: -c.u[1], z: -c.u[2] }),\n1407\t      U * .5 + T.ride + T.reach, true);\n1408\t    if (h) hits.push({ point: add(o, c.u, -h.timeOfImpact), normal: [h.normal.x, h.normal.y, h.normal.z], d: h.timeOfImpact - U * .5 });\n1409\t  }\n1410\t  return hits;\n1411\t}\n1412\tfunction step(c, ctl, dt, G) {\n1413\t  const g = [0, 0, -G], hits = probe(c);\n1414\t  let n = null, d = 0;\n1415\t  if (hits.length === 4) { n = norm(cross(add(hits[1].point, hits[2].point, -1), add(hits[0].point, hits[3].point, -1))); if (dot(n, c.u) < 0) n = n.map(x => -x); }\n1416\t  else if (hits.length >= 2) n = norm(hits.reduce((s, h) => add(s, h.normal), [0, 0, 0]));\n1417\t  if (n) d = hits.reduce((s, h) => s + h.d, 0) / hits.length;\n1418\t  if (n) {\n1419\t    const vn = dot(c.v, n), pull = dot(g, n);                              // pull > 0: gravity pulls the car off\n1420\t    const k0 = c.grounded ? -dot(add(n, c.n, -1), norm(c.v)) / Math.max(1, len(c.v) * dt) : 0;\n1421\t    c.kappa = c.grounded ? c.kappa + (k0 - c.kappa) * Math.min(1, dt / .04) : 0;\n1422\t    const vt2 = Math.max(0, len(c.v) ** 2 - vn * vn);\n1423\t    const aEff = T.adhesion * Math.min(1, Math.sqrt(vt2) / (15 * U));       // adhesion fades out below 15 m/s\n1424\t    c.load = vt2 * c.kappa - pull + aEff;                                   // normal load per unit mass\n1425\t    c.slip = c.load >= 0 ? 0 : c.slip + dt;\n1426\t    c.grounded = c.grounded ? (c.slip < .06 && d < T.ride + T.reach) : (vn < 0 && d < T.ride + T.reach * .6);\n1427\t  } else c.grounded = false;\n1428\t  if (c.grounded) {\n1429\t    c.u = norm(add(c.u, add(n, c.u, -1), Math.min(1, T.align * dt)));\n1430\t    c.f = norm(add(c.f, c.u, -dot(c.f, c.u)));\n1431\t    c.v = add(c.v, n, -dot(c.v, n));\n1432\t    const traction = T.mu * Math.max(0, c.load);                            // what the tyres can pass on (μ·N/m)\n1433\t    let a = add(g, n, -dot(g, n));\n1434\t    const sp = dot(c.v, c.f);\n1435\t    if (ctl.gas) a = add(a, c.f, Math.min(traction, T.A0 * Math.max(0, 1 - (Math.max(0, sp) / T.vtop) ** 1.6)));\n1436\t    a = add(a, c.v, -T.cd * len(c.v));\n1437\t    const r = cross(c.u, c.f), vl = dot(c.v, r), maxDv = traction * dt;    // (§4.4's grip model replaces this line)\n1438\t    c.v = add(c.v, r, -Math.max(-maxDv, Math.min(maxDv, vl * Math.min(1, 12 * dt))));\n1439\t    c.v = add(c.v, a, dt); c.p = add(c.p, c.v, dt);\n1440\t    c.p = add(c.p, n, (T.ride - d) * Math.min(1, 25 * dt));\n1441\t    c.n = n;\n1442\t  } else {\n1443\t    c.v = add(c.v, g, dt); c.v = add(c.v, c.v, -T.cd * .3 * len(c.v) * dt); c.p = add(c.p, c.v, dt);\n1444\t    c.f = norm(add(c.f, add(norm(c.v), c.f, -1), Math.min(1, 1.5 * dt)));\n1445\t    const r = norm(cross(c.u, c.f)); c.u = norm(cross(c.f, r)); c.n = c.u;\n1446\t  }\n1447\t}\n1448\t// state: { p, v: [0,0,0], f: [1,0,0], u: [0,0,1], n: [0,0,1], grounded: false, kappa: 0, slip: 0, load: 0 }\n1449\t// Track ribbons are triangles wound so (b−a)×(c−a) points along the surface's up in engine axes; after adding\n1450\t// colliders, call pw.step() once so ray queries see them.\n1451\t```\n1452\t\n1453\t## Appendix B — what was verified during planning (so you can trust it)\n1454\t\n1455\t| Claim | How it was checked |\n1456\t| --- | --- |\n1457\t| The 3D engine, three r182 and Rapier 0.19.3 load and step headless in Node 24 | §9.1 loader run against a copy of the engine files: a terrain `World3D` built, stepped by `game.advance(1)`, `world.hash()` returned, 0 errors |\n1458\t| The single-file bundle runs from `file://` | §2.7 pipeline, Playwright 1.63 Chromium: booted, WebGL 2, 0 errors, picture drawn |\n1459\t| The car model holds loops and lands jumps | Appendix A, extracted from this file and run in Node with Rapier trimesh ribbons: loop thresholds and kicker landings as listed under §4.4 \"Prototype results\" |\n1460\t| A sprung Rapier rigid body bounces off the loop | Spring-damper raycast wheels on a dynamic cuboid launched into the air at the loop entry at 150 km/h (and bottomed out with strong downforce) |\n1461\t| Rapier JS result field names | §4.3 list from a probe (`timeOfImpact` vs `time_of_impact` differ by query) |\n1462\t| All 15 track programs and 6 puzzle solutions fit the grid with no overlaps | a grid walker implementing §6.1's rules |\n1463\t| AI Hub protocol, metas, harness checks | read from `ai-hub/lib/hub/README.md`, `session.js`, `harness.html`, `examples/ghost.html` at commit f8835e4 |\n1464\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66d97bf5-dd15-40b7-85f8-8eecadfc963f","uuid":"7898f750-9340-4a53-b597-cbf5649b36e8","timestamp":"2026-11-04T12:03:43.135Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-xhigh.build__20261104-050308__x1f94fb/work/PLAN.md","content":"// tools/node-env.mjs — the engine, the 3D engine and the game in Node, no browser\nimport { registerHooks } from 'node:module';\nimport { pathToFileURL, fileURLToPath } from 'node:url';\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nconst ROOT = fileURLToPath(new URL('..', import.meta.url)), V = ROOT + 'engine/vendor/';\nconst MAP = { 'three': 'three-0.182.0/three.webgpu.min.js', 'three/webgpu': 'three-0.182.0/three.webgpu.min.js',\n  'three/tsl': 'three-0.182.0/three.tsl.min.js', '@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat': 'rapier3d-simd-compat-0.19.3/rapier.js' };\nregisterHooks({ resolve: (spec, ctx, next) => MAP[spec] ? { url: pathToFileURL(V + MAP[spec]).href, format: 'module', shortCircuit: true } : next(spec, ctx) });\nvm.runInThisContext(readFileSync(ROOT + 'engine/my-3d2dge.js', 'utf8'), { filename: 'my-3d2dge.js' });  // globalThis.My3D2dge\nexport const E = globalThis.My3D2dge;\n// World3D bakes textures on canvases: hand it the 2D engine's headless stand-in canvas\nconst standIn = () => { const d = globalThis.document; delete globalThis.document; const c = E.mkCanvas(1, 1); globalThis.document = d; return c; };\nglobalThis.document = { createElement: standIn, getElementById: () => null, querySelector: () => null, addEventListener() {}, removeEventListener() {} };\nawait import(pathToFileURL(ROOT + 'engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js').href);                                   // E.World3D, E.THREE, E.RAPIER\nexport async function makeGame(o = {}) {\n  const { createGame } = await import(pathToFileURL(ROOT + 'src/main.js').href);\n  const g = await createGame({ headless: true, ...o }); await g.game.booted; return g;                 // { game, api }\n}\n```\nIn Node, `new E.Game({ headless: true })` has no screen and skips `draw`; `E.World3D.init(game)` returns after\n`RAPIER.init()` without a renderer; worlds build their meshes but never render. Rapier prints a harmless \"deprecated\nparameters\" warning on init — filter it from test output.\n\n### 9.2 The one command\n\n`node tools/test.mjs [suite ...] [--browser] [--hub] [--all]` loads the engine once, runs the suites in-process, and\nprints **only** `FAIL <suite>: <check>: <detail>` lines and one summary line (`247 checks, 0 failed, 12.4 s`); exit\ncode 1 on any failure. `--browser` adds §9.5, `--hub` adds §9.6, `--all` both. Each suite lists the source files it\ncovers (`covers: ['src/car/**', 'src/track/**']`) so you rerun only what a change touches. Use `game.advance(s)`,\n`input.hold/tap/press`, `game.debug.snapshot()` and the `api` handle (load track, place car, run bot, editor\noperations, fake AI Hub) — the engine's `game/test.mjs` pattern.\n\n`game.debug.snapshot()` returns at least: `{ scene, page, mode, env, track, run: { phase, steps, cps, cpTotal,\nrespawns, finished, medal }, car: { x, y, z, kmh, grounded, surface, block, up }, profile: { coppers, medals, unlocked\n}, ui: { focus, prompt }, attract, touchGate, hub: { active, phase }, errors: game.errors.length }`.\n\n### 9.3 Suites and what they check\n\n| Suite | Checks (each a named check) |\n| --- | --- |\n| `turtle` | every track and puzzle program compiles; no overlaps; in bounds; expected CP counts; kicker→landing links; puzzle fixed blocks equal the solution's ST/CP/FN cells; inventories cover the solutions |\n| `blocks` | every block type: path is C0/C1 continuous (Δp < 1 cm, Δt < 0.5° between samples), unit t/u, u ⊥ t; mesh has no NaN; Rapier winding normals agree with u (dot > 0.5) and three winding is the reverse; **every link in every shipped track**: port frames match (1 cm, 0.5°) |\n| `physics` | (Coyote unless noted) 0→100 km/h in 2.3–3.3 s; reaches ≥ 97% vtop on a long straight; 100→0 braking in 12–22 m; R2 at 90 km/h holds the lane, R2 at 130 km/h and R1 at 80 km/h run wide (they need braking); BR2 holds at 150 km/h; **loop block on full throttle from ≥ 60 km/h: grounded all the way, exits upright; from ≤ 40 km/h: detaches at the top; coasting from ≥ 115 km/h holds, ≤ 95 km/h fails** (re-measure and update these numbers if tuning changes); ice: acceleration capped by traction (≤ 0.35 × asphalt's from standstill); U1 crest at 120 km/h: airborne; kicker at the D2 approach: lands on the landing; wall at 100 km/h at 30°: no penetration, speed kept 40–90%; ice cornering speed < 70% of asphalt's; boost pad adds ≥ 9 m/s; flop recovers upright within 1 s; respawn → at the CP, v = 0, upright; 10 s of identical inputs twice → identical state hash |\n| `race` | CPs count once each, in any order, either direction; finish refused before all CPs (\"MISSING CHECKPOINT\"); clock runs through respawns; restart resets; splits and deltas vs best; medal thresholds from author (1.06/1.2/1.5 with rounding); results rewards paid once per tier; records saved |\n| `ghost` | a recorded bot run plays back within 2 cm / 1° of the live car at every sample; encode/decode round trip exact; size < 25 KB/min |\n| `bot` | skill 1 finishes all 15 tracks and 6 puzzle solutions with 0 respawns; steps equal `medals.json` (±1); skill 0.8 finishes slower; speed plan reaches every gap's required speed |\n| `campaign` | unlock rules (D1–D2 open; next on medal; puzzles/survival/env gates); coppers ledger (rewards, block costs, refunds, packs, patterns); story beats fire once; profile save/load/migrate |\n| `editor` | place/rotate/raise/remove with occupancy and costs; refuse overlaps, out-of-grid, unaffordable; kicker reserves its gap; undo/redo 50 random ops returns to the same state and coppers; validate (bot drive) sets author + medals; any edit clears validation; save/load slots; share code round trip; export-as-content output compiles |\n| `puzzle` | fixed blocks locked; inventory counts enforced; zone and no-build cells enforced; each reference solution placed through the editor API validates and earns at least Gold at skill 1 |\n| `survival` | rival runs deterministic per gauntlet+round; placing rules (+2/+1/0/out); rank names; elimination ends the run; clearing pays once |\n| `hotseat` | 3 players × 2 attempts × 2 tracks with scripted bot turns → correct standings and points; pass-the-controller cards between turns |\n| `split` | 2 and 4 players: viewports and cameras created and removed; each car finishes; HUD per viewport; no car–car collisions |\n| `online` | with a **fake AIHub** object (connect → info, card events, start, time, send/receive, time-up, end, leave): no title/menus; `ready()` once without input; Enter answers ready on our card; ghost messages ≤ 10/s and < 1 KB; progress each second; exactly one `result`; input and sound stop on `end`; outside a session nothing changes |\n| `ui` | title → menu → every page reachable by keys only and by simulated mouse clicks (`input.feed`), and back; focus never lost; prompt glyphs switch keyboard ↔ gamepad (PlayStation) ↔ Xbox setting; Dev Mode opens from the pause menu, a slider changes `CFG` live, Reset restores defaults; attract starts after 10 s idle on title and on the main menu, not in the editor; any input exits; touch-only flag shows the gate with Settings |\n| `playthrough` | **the whole game, scripted**: fresh profile → welcome beat → all 15 races driven by the bot as the player through the real menus (pressing the real buttons) → medals, coppers and unlocks as designed → the 6 puzzles solved through the editor UI → each gauntlet run (bot at skill 1 clears it) → build and validate a 12-block track in the editor, save, reload, share code → paint a car in the garage → save and reopen a replay → hot seat (2 players) and split screen (2 players) races → golds everywhere → ending beat and credits → final profile matches expectations; 0 engine errors |\n\n### 9.4 Rules for testing\n\n- Keep checks state-based (snapshot fields, profile values, physics numbers). Use screenshots only for looks.\n- Rerun a suite only after changing code it covers; run `--all` before each milestone exit and at the end.\n- Don't use subagents or workflows to review, judge or audit (TASK.md). Fix the first failure first.\n\n### 9.5 Browser checks (`tools/browser.mjs`, Playwright 1.63 + Chromium; built HTML opened from `file://`)\n\nLaunch Chromium with `--use-angle=swiftshader --enable-unsafe-swiftshader --ignore-gpu-blocklist\n--autoplay-policy=no-user-gesture-required`. Checks: no page errors or console errors; boot finishes within 60 s;\n`window.__crack.snapshot().scene === 'title'`; the canvas is not blank (pixel variance); `?backend=webgl` also boots;\ndeep links `#race/D3`, `#race/R3`, `#race/S3`, `#editor`, `#puzzle/PD2`, `#survival/hedgerow`, `#split/2/S2`,\n`#garage`, `#replay/last`, `#about`, `#lab/physics`, `#lab/blocks` each reach their scene; the bot's D1 and D3 times in\nthe browser equal `medals.json` (determinism Node ↔ browser); attract starts after 10 s idle and a key press ends it;\na touch-only context (`hasTouch: true, isMobile: true`, 390×844) shows the gate text and the Settings button and runs\nattract. Screenshots to `check-output/` for review: title, each environment at a signature spot (D3 loop, D5 canyon\njump mid-air, R3 crossing, S3 drop, Frostpeak lamps), HUD at a CP split, results with a medal, editor with palette,\npuzzle zone, survival standings, split screen ×4, garage, replay TV cam, Dev Mode, About. The engine's\n`tools/check.mjs` also works on the built file (`node engine/tools/check.mjs <file>#race/D3`) — act on its look notes.\n\n### 9.6 AI Hub harness (`tools/hub.mjs`)\n\nCopy `harness.html`, `bridge.js`, `round.js` and the built HTML (as `game.html`) into `<devfolder>/.hubtest/`;\nstart `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory .hubtest`, read the port it prints, fetch `game.html`\nand confirm its `<title>` is CRACKMANIA (it's ours, not another agent's server); then in Playwright open\n`harness.html?game=game.html&players=2&auto=1&limit=45`, wait for `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'`, require\n`window.__hubCheck.pass === true`; repeat with `players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1&limit=45` and with\n`&scenario=host-leave`. Print failing checks' names and details. Stop the server by its PID. (The round respects\n`info.limitMs`: end the time attack 5 s before it when shorter than 3 minutes.)\n\n---\n\n## 10. Build order and milestones\n\nEach milestone ends with its exit checks green (`node tools/test.mjs <its suites>`), a build, and a short look in the\nbrowser. Do them in order — later ones lean on earlier ones (the bot in M3 is what tests everything after it).\n\n| M | Scope | Exit |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **M0 Foundations** (de-risk first) | dev folder, engine copy (§2.2), engine changes E1–E6, `package.json`, `node-env.mjs`, `test.mjs` skeleton, `build.mjs`; a Dustbowl world (terrain, sky, sun, fog), one straight block mesh, a pen box car, HUD text | headless boot test green; the built single HTML opens from `file://` in headless Chromium with no errors and a non-blank 3D picture under the HUD |\n| **M1 Drive** | blocks ST/FN/CP/S/turns/hills; ribbon mesher, cross-sections, base plate, boundary, colliders; CarSim complete (§4.4); far/close/hood cameras; Coyote model; minimal HUD | `physics` (flat, turns, crest, walls, determinism), `blocks` for those types; D1 drivable |\n| **M2 Stunts + catalogue** | kicker/gap/landing/chasm, loop + lane assist, boost, banked, crossing, bumps, dirt/ice/snow, supports, rails; turtle compiler; all 15 tracks; `#lab/blocks`, `#lab/physics` | `turtle`, `blocks`, loop/jump `physics` checks; screenshots of every track |\n| **M3 Racing** | run rules, gates, respawn/restart, splits, basic results; ghosts; bot; `bake.mjs`; `medals.json` | `race`, `ghost`, `bot` |\n| **M4 Worlds and art** | three environments (terrain, sky, plate textures, palettes), Pebble and Moose, paint system, deco + trackside dressing, new shapes, animated props, FX, Drapeau, crowd, gates' boards and lights | screenshots reviewed (§9.5 list); check.mjs look notes handled |\n| **M5 Sound** | car synth, SFX, songs, stings, babble | headless no-op verified; manual listen in browser; mute/volume honoured |\n| **M6 Front end + campaign** | UI kit, glyphs, prompt bar, title, menus, env/track select, results, profile, unlocks, coppers, story beats, tips, settings, per-scene pause items | `ui` (minus attract/dev), `campaign` |\n| **M7 Editor + Puzzle** | editor scene, controls, palette, packs, undo/redo, test drive, validate, slots, codes, export; puzzle mode; 6 puzzles | `editor`, `puzzle` |\n| **M8 Modes** | Survival, Hot Seat, Split Screen, Replays, Garage | `survival`, `hotseat`, `split`, replay/garage checks in `ui` |\n| **M9 Online** | AI Hub ghost mode, own card | `online`; `--hub` all three runs pass |\n| **M10 Shell features** | Dev Mode, attract mode, touch gate, About/Credits, ending + credits roll | full `ui`; `--browser` |\n| **M11 Finish** | `playthrough`; balance pass with Dev sliders (re-bake medals); polish; final build; About texts; `exit-interview.json`; final reply | `node tools/test.mjs --all` green; deliverables in place (§12) |\n\n---\n\n## 11. Risks and how to de-risk them\n\n| Risk | Mitigation |\n| --- | --- |\n| Car physics through loops/jumps feels wrong or is unstable | Build exactly the validated model (§4.4, Appendix A); keep the four-point plane fit, the curvature filter and the 0.06 s detach grace; lane assist on loops; physics tests encode the intended behaviour (fast holds, slow falls); `#lab/physics` and live sliders for tuning; re-bake medals after tuning |\n| Bundling three + Rapier + the ESM 3D engine into one file that runs from `file://` | Prove it in M0 before anything else; esbuild plugin resolution; escape `</script`; fallback import map to jsDelivr (allowed) |\n| Headless testing of a 3D engine | The loader in §9.1 was run successfully during planning; keep pure logic (track model, CarSim, run, bot, economy, editor ops) free of three.js calls so most suites don't depend on rendering at all |\n| Block seams (cracks, bumps, wrong normals at joints) | Shared exact port frames; per-link tests; ribbons sample the exact end points; `#lab/blocks` shows every block in a row |\n| Bot can't drive some track (bake, Survival, attract and tests all depend on it) | Route window search (no lane jumping in loops), recovery rules, speed plan that knows gaps; the `bot` suite over all content; skill 1 must finish with 0 respawns — if not, fix the track (add a boost, widen a bend) rather than the bot |\n| Node vs browser determinism of baked times | No wall-clock or renderer reads in simulation; same V8 + same Rapier WASM; browser check compares D1/D3 times |\n| Editor is clumsy on a pad at 10 feet | Build cursor + palette first in M7 and try: a 10-block track with only the pad in under 2 minutes; mouse parity (hover picks cells); big icons; red/green preview |\n| AI Hub conformance | All session code in `modes/online.js`; fake-hub unit suite; the real harness in three configurations; README rules as a checklist |\n| Shader stalls on track load / editing | All materials and pen batches (incl. ghost) made at boot; `world.prepare()`; only geometry changes later; dispose old geometries |\n| WebGPU vs WebGL 2 | three falls back by itself; test `?backend=webgl`; never read back from the GPU (engine rule) |\n| Scope | Build each feature's minimal complete form end to end first (e.g. garage with colours and 3 patterns), then deepen; nothing ships half-done |\n| Shared machine, full `/tmp` | Caches and temp files inside the dev folder; only your own PIDs; servers on 127.0.0.1 with an OS port |\n\n---\n\n## 12. Finishing: deliverables, About, exit interview, final reply\n\n- `Crackmania-TrackMania2003-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174810.html` in the root (beside TASK.md), built by\n  `node tools/build.mjs` from a clean checkout of the dev folder; opens from `file://` with no errors; passes the hub\n  harness; title screen reads **CRACKMANIA**.\n- The dev folder holds everything needed to rebuild and retest (`npm install`, `node tools/test.mjs --all`,\n  `node tools/build.mjs`); `engine/CHANGES.md` lists E1–E6 and anything else changed, with the reason.\n- About/Credits pages and the final chat reply carry the same **Source Information** (Date `2026-11-03 17:48:10`;\n  Source `TrackMania (2003, Nadeo)`; Plan `PLAN.md`; Genre and Perspective `Arcade racing (time attack) and\n  track-building puzzle; third-person chase camera, orbiting editor camera`; Tech `my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (2D engine + 3D\n  engine), three.js r182 (WebGPU/WebGL 2), Rapier 0.19.3, esbuild (build), Playwright 1.63 (tests)`; Art Direction\n  `the engine's native low-res toon 3D with ink outlines and code-drawn pixel textures`; Animation `engine rigs, poses,\n  tweens and scripts plus code-driven car/prop animation`; Audio `engine chip synth songs, WebAudio car synth, Animalese-\n  style gibberish voices`; Online `AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode`; Testing `headless Node suites with\n  game.advance/game.debug, a scripted whole-game playthrough, Playwright checks of the built file, the AI Hub\n  harness`; Research `what you actually did`; Environment `Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown`; Model\n  `Anthropic, <your model id>, reasoning effort <yours>`; Usage `estimates or \"unknown\"`) and the answers to the\n  **Testing / Engine / Prompt Feedback** questions (TASK.md lists them).\n- `exit-interview.json` beside the HTML, in TASK.md's exact shape, every value filled, plain text, checked with\n  `node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json','utf8'))\"`. Suggested `aiHub` block:\n  `name` \"CRACKMANIA\", `tagline` \"Crack the clock.\", `description` \"Block-built stunt tracks, loops and canyon jumps\n  against the clock: race, solve track puzzles, survive the Ghost Guild and build your own tracks.\", `type` \"Game\",\n  `genre` \"Racing\", `source` \"TrackMania (2003)\", `series` \"TrackMania\", `players` \"1–4\", `controls` \"R2/W gas, L2/S\n  brake, left stick/arrows steer, Circle/Enter respawn, Triangle/Delete restart\", `tags` [\"3d\", \"arcade\", \"vehicles\",\n  \"versus\", \"retro\", \"low-poly\"].\n- Final reply: a short summary of the game plus the four information blocks above.\n\n---\n\n## Appendix A — the validated car core (reference code from the planning spike)\n\nEngine units (`U = 16` per metre), z up, `dt = 1/120`. `pw` is TrackPhysics' Rapier world (fixed trimesh colliders\nonly), `RAPIER` the module (`E.RAPIER`). This exact code produced §4.4's prototype results; §4.4 adds steering, the\ngrip/drift model, surfaces, boost, walls, flop, landing loss and lane assist on top of it. Vectors are `[x, y, z]`\narrays.\n\n```js\nconst cross = (a, b) => [a[1]*b[2]-a[2]*b[1], a[2]*b[0]-a[0]*b[2], a[0]*b[1]-a[1]*b[0]];\nconst add = (a, b, k = 1) => [a[0]+b[0]*k, a[1]+b[1]*k, a[2]+b[2]*k], dot = (a, b) => a[0]*b[0]+a[1]*b[1]+a[2]*b[2];\nconst len = a => Math.hypot(a[0], a[1], a[2]), norm = a => { const l = len(a) || 1; return [a[0]/l, a[1]/l, a[2]/l]; };\n// Coyote-like tuning in engine units (cd: 0.0004 per metre = 0.0004/U per unit)\nconst T = { ride: .55*U, reach: .9*U, A0: 12*U, vtop: 64*U, cd: .0004/U, adhesion: .35*9.81*U, align: 30, mu: 1 };\nconst WHEELS = [[1.35*U, -.8*U], [1.35*U, .8*U], [-1.35*U, -.8*U], [-1.35*U, .8*U]];   // FL, FR, RL, RR (right = +y)\nfunction probe(c) {\n  const r = cross(c.u, c.f), hits = [];\n  for (const [lx, ly] of WHEELS) {\n    const o = add(add(add(c.p, c.f, lx), r, ly), c.u, U * .5);            // from half a metre above the floor\n    const h = pw.castRayAndGetNormal(new RAPIER.Ray({ x: o[0], y: o[1], z: o[2] }, { x: -c.u[0], y: -c.u[1], z: -c.u[2] }),\n      U * .5 + T.ride + T.reach, true);\n    if (h) hits.push({ point: add(o, c.u, -h.timeOfImpact), normal: [h.normal.x, h.normal.y, h.normal.z], d: h.timeOfImpact - U * .5 });\n  }\n  return hits;\n}\nfunction step(c, ctl, dt, G) {\n  const g = [0, 0, -G], hits = probe(c);\n  let n = null, d = 0;\n  if (hits.length === 4) { n = norm(cross(add(hits[1].point, hits[2].point, -1), add(hits[0].point, hits[3].point, -1))); if (dot(n, c.u) < 0) n = n.map(x => -x); }\n  else if (hits.length >= 2) n = norm(hits.reduce((s, h) => add(s, h.normal), [0, 0, 0]));\n  if (n) d = hits.reduce((s, h) => s + h.d, 0) / hits.length;\n  if (n) {\n    const vn = dot(c.v, n), pull = dot(g, n);                              // pull > 0: gravity pulls the car off\n    const k0 = c.grounded ? -dot(add(n, c.n, -1), norm(c.v)) / Math.max(1, len(c.v) * dt) : 0;\n    c.kappa = c.grounded ? c.kappa + (k0 - c.kappa) * Math.min(1, dt / .04) : 0;\n    const vt2 = Math.max(0, len(c.v) ** 2 - vn * vn);\n    const aEff = T.adhesion * Math.min(1, Math.sqrt(vt2) / (15 * U));       // adhesion fades out below 15 m/s\n    c.load = vt2 * c.kappa - pull + aEff;                                   // normal load per unit mass\n    c.slip = c.load >= 0 ? 0 : c.slip + dt;\n    c.grounded = c.grounded ? (c.slip < .06 && d < T.ride + T.reach) : (vn < 0 && d < T.ride + T.reach * .6);\n  } else c.grounded = false;\n  if (c.grounded) {\n    c.u = norm(add(c.u, add(n, c.u, -1), Math.min(1, T.align * dt)));\n    c.f = norm(add(c.f, c.u, -dot(c.f, c.u)));\n    c.v = add(c.v, n, -dot(c.v, n));\n    const traction = T.mu * Math.max(0, c.load);                            // what the tyres can pass on (μ·N/m)\n    let a = add(g, n, -dot(g, n));\n    const sp = dot(c.v, c.f);\n    if (ctl.gas) a = add(a, c.f, Math.min(traction, T.A0 * Math.max(0, 1 - (Math.max(0, sp) / T.vtop) ** 1.6)));\n    a = add(a, c.v, -T.cd * len(c.v));\n    const r = cross(c.u, c.f), vl = dot(c.v, r), maxDv = traction * dt;    // (§4.4's grip model replaces this line)\n    c.v = add(c.v, r, -Math.max(-maxDv, Math.min(maxDv, vl * Math.min(1, 12 * dt))));\n    c.v = add(c.v, a, dt); c.p = add(c.p, c.v, dt);\n    c.p = add(c.p, n, (T.ride - d) * Math.min(1, 25 * dt));\n    c.n = n;\n  } else {\n    c.v = add(c.v, g, dt); c.v = add(c.v, c.v, -T.cd * .3 * len(c.v) * dt); c.p = add(c.p, c.v, dt);\n    c.f = norm(add(c.f, add(norm(c.v), c.f, -1), Math.min(1, 1.5 * dt)));\n    const r = norm(cross(c.u, c.f)); c.u = norm(cross(c.f, r)); c.n = c.u;\n  }\n}\n// state: { p, v: [0,0,0], f: [1,0,0], u: [0,0,1], n: [0,0,1], grounded: false, kappa: 0, slip: 0, load: 0 }\n// Track ribbons are triangles wound so (b−a)×(c−a) points along the surface's up in engine axes; after adding\n// colliders, call pw.step() once so ray queries see them.\n```\n\n## Appendix B — what was verified during planning (so you can trust it)\n\n| Claim | How it was checked |\n| --- | --- |\n| The 3D engine, three r182 and Rapier 0.19.3 load and step headless in Node 24 | §9.1 loader run against a copy of the engine files: a terrain `World3D` built, stepped by `game.advance(1)`, `world.hash()` returned, 0 errors |\n| The single-file bundle runs from `file://` | §2.7 pipeline, Playwright 1.63 Chromium: booted, WebGL 2, 0 errors, picture drawn |\n| The car model holds loops and lands jumps | Appendix A, extracted from this file and run in Node with Rapier trimesh ribbons: loop thresholds and kicker landings as listed under §4.4 \"Prototype results\" |\n| A sprung Rapier rigid body bounces off the loop | Spring-damper raycast wheels on a dynamic cuboid launched into the air at the loop entry at 150 km/h (and bottomed out with strong downforce) |\n| Rapier JS result field names | §4.3 list from a probe (`timeOfImpact` vs `time_of_impact` differ by query) |\n| All 15 track programs and 6 puzzle solutions fit the grid with no overlaps | a grid walker implementing §6.1's rules |\n| AI Hub protocol, metas, harness checks | read from `ai-hub/lib/hub/README.md`, `session.js`, `harness.html`, `examples/ghost.html` at commit f8835e4 |\n","numLines":236,"startLine":1229,"totalLines":1464}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018t2i22iq3Hr3KunW4QpAcX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
