{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghxRRdQkmvudM1h6XGUR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TLtTHBmDRjkhGjxpPBmHEb","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/scenes/race.js'; s=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"  for (const Q of sess.players) {\n    if (Q.hidden) continue;\n    const ghostly = sess.players.length > 1 && Q !== P;   // (split screen: the others are ghosts to you)\n    drawRunCar(pen, Q, alpha, ghostly, t);\n  }\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"  for (const Q of sess.players) {\n    if (Q.hidden) continue;\n    const ghostly = sess.players.length > 1 && Q !== P;   // (split screen: the others are ghosts to you)\n    if (Q === P && P.cam.mode === 'hood' && S.phase !== 'intro' && !(ctx.dev && ctx.dev.freeCam) && !(P.run.finished && S.finishT > 0)) { drawBonnet(pen, Q, alpha, t); continue; }\n    drawRunCar(pen, Q, alpha, ghostly, t);\n  }\"\"\"\nassert old in s\ns=s.replace(old,new)\ns=s.replace(\"export function drawRunCar(pen, Q, alpha, ghostly, t) {\",\"\"\"/** the hood camera: your own car is the bonnet below the eye and a strip of dashboard (its paint, its lights) */\nfunction drawBonnet(pen, Q, alpha, t) {\n  const car = Q.run.car, L = Q._lastStep; let p = car.p, f = car.f, u = car.u;\n  if (L && alpha < 1) { p = lerp3(L.p, car.p, alpha); f = norm(lerp3(L.f, car.f, alpha)); u = norm(lerp3(L.u, car.u, alpha)); }\n  const r = cross(u, f), paint = Q.paint || {}, body = paint.body || '#e8402a';\n  pen.frame(p[0] * U, p[1] * U, p[2] * U, f, r, u, U);\n  pen.slab(.75, 0, .78, 2.3, 0, .62, 0, 1, 0, 1.7, .12, body).box(2.25, 0, .55, .12, 1.8, .25, '#2a2a30');\n  if (paint.pattern === 1) for (const sd of [-1, 1]) pen.slab(.76, sd * .22, .85, 2.3, sd * .22, .69, 0, 1, 0, .16, .03, paint.patternColor || '#ffffff');\n  pen.box(.55, 0, .86, .2, 1.8, .1, '#1a1a22');\n  if (ENVS[S.session.env].lights) for (const sd of [-1, 1]) pen.glow(2.4, sd * .7, .5, .25, '#fff4c0');\n  pen.at();\n}\nexport function drawRunCar(pen, Q, alpha, ghostly, t) {\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ncat > engine/CHANGES.md <<'EOF'\n# Changes to my-3D2dge v0.85.2 made for CRACKMANIA\n\nEach change is marked `CRACKMANIA (En)` in the source.\n\n| # | File | Change | Why |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| E1 | `my-3d2dge-3d.js`, `class Pen` | `pen.frame(x, y, z, f, r, u, k)`: the pen's frame from orthonormal axes | draw a car in any orientation (upside down in a loop) without Euler angles |\n| E2 | `my-3d2dge-3d.js`, `Camera3D.place()` | a pose may carry `up: [x, y, z]` (engine axes) and `look: [x, y, z]` (a point); roll is skipped when `up` is given | a chase camera that follows the car round a loop; poses set as a look-at |\n| E3 | `my-3d2dge-3d.js`, `makeBatches()`, `Pen` | a second set of tube / ball / box / cone batches in a translucent toon material (no outline shell); `pen.ghost = true` routes parts into them | translucent ghost cars; made with the world, so no shader is built mid-game |\n| E4 | `my-3d2dge.js`, `Input.tick`, `Input.analog()` | the pad's button values are kept (`padValues`); `input.analog(action)` is the strongest of the action's codes (an analog trigger's value, 1 for keys) | analog R2 / L2 throttle and brake |\n| E5 | `my-3d2dge.js`, input + settings | PlayStation glyphs by default; the Button symbols setting offers PlayStation and Xbox and applies to every player | TASK.md: PlayStation glyphs, Xbox as the option |\n| E6 | `my-3d2dge-3d.js`, statics | `World3D.TOON_BANDS` exported | track and prop materials in the pen's own toon bands |\n| E7 | `my-3d2dge-3d.js`, `World3D.draw()` | `world.particleGround` overrides the particles' ground query | the terrain sits 60 m under the track's plate: dust and sparks land on the plate |\n| E8 | `my-3d2dge.js`, the 5x7 font | glyphs `· ✓ ◀ ▶ ▲ ▼ ¢ — … ★ ↻` | the UI's ticks, choice arrows, the copper sign |\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Draw a bonnet in hood view and document engine changes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}