{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghyuEpAqd8zHbDibDB4P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"While the hub harness runs (I'm keeping the CPU free for it), writing a short README for the dev folder."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":422,"cache_read_input_tokens":848924,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":422},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66d97bf5-dd15-40b7-85f8-8eecadfc963f","uuid":"e2f6d468-548e-446c-9ca0-d98d2448e979","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:39:53.814Z","request_id":"req_011CghyuENPY2fQrhiEU4mKE"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghyuEpAqd8zHbDibDB4P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DVzWNi8XmDyo43VjVyiDt6","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# CRACKMANIA — dev folder\n\nAn original arcade time-attack stunt racer inspired by TrackMania (2003), built on my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (2D engine + 3D\nengine, three.js r182, Rapier 0.19.3). The playable single file is `../Crackmania-TrackMania2003-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050308.html`.\n\n```sh\nnpm install                      # esbuild + Playwright (Chromium is expected in the Playwright cache)\nnode tools/build.mjs             # -> the single HTML file in the parent folder\nnode tools/test.mjs              # every headless suite; prints only failures and one count line\nnode tools/test.mjs --browser    # + Playwright checks of the built file from file://\nnode tools/test.mjs --hub        # + the AI Hub harness (2 players; 4 with latency and loss; host leaving)\nnode tools/bake.mjs              # re-bake the author times (src/data/medals.js) after a tuning change\nnode tools/shot.mjs '#race/D3' name 6000   # a screenshot of a deep link into check-output/\nnode tools/exit-interview.mjs    # ../exit-interview.json from src/data/about.js\n```\n\nDeep links: `#race/D3`, `#editor`, `#puzzle/PD2`, `#survival/hedgerow`, `#split/2/S2`, `#hotseat/D1`, `#garage`,\n`#replay/last`, `#about`, `#credits`, `#attract`, `#lab/blocks`, `#lab/physics`, `#menu/<page>`.\n\nLayout: `engine/` (the engine, its docs and tools; `engine/CHANGES.md` lists what was changed), `hub/session.js` (AI Hub\nclient, verbatim), `src/` (the game: `track/` blocks, mesher, physics, scenery; `car/` simulation, drawing, cameras;\n`race/` runs, ghosts, the bot, medals; `modes/`, `scenes/`, `editor/`, `ui/`, `audio/`, `story/`, `data/`), `tools/`\n(build, tests, bake, browser and hub checks). New content: add a turtle program to `src/data/tracks.js` (or export one\nfrom the editor's Dev Mode), then `node tools/bake.mjs`.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Write the dev folder README"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":422,"cache_read_input_tokens":848924,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":422},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"66d97bf5-dd15-40b7-85f8-8eecadfc963f","uuid":"a077da42-4051-4d09-ae02-902102e57aaf","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:40:00.983Z","request_id":"req_011CghyuENPY2fQrhiEU4mKE","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01DVzWNi8XmDyo43VjVyiDt6":{"command":"cat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# CRACKMANIA — dev folder\n\nAn original arcade time-attack stunt racer inspired by TrackMania (2003), built on my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (2D engine + 3D\nengine, three.js r182, Rapier 0.19.3). The playable single file is `../Crackmania-TrackMania2003-claude-opus-5-5-xhigh-20261104-050308.html`.\n\n```sh\nnpm install                      # esbuild + Playwright (Chromium is expected in the Playwright cache)\nnode tools/build.mjs             # -> the single HTML file in the parent folder\nnode tools/test.mjs              # every headless suite; prints only failures and one count line\nnode tools/test.mjs --browser    # + Playwright checks of the built file from file://\nnode tools/test.mjs --hub        # + the AI Hub harness (2 players; 4 with latency and loss; host leaving)\nnode tools/bake.mjs              # re-bake the author times (src/data/medals.js) after a tuning change\nnode tools/shot.mjs '#race/D3' name 6000   # a screenshot of a deep link into check-output/\nnode tools/exit-interview.mjs    # ../exit-interview.json from src/data/about.js\n```\n\nDeep links: `#race/D3`, `#editor`, `#puzzle/PD2`, `#survival/hedgerow`, `#split/2/S2`, `#hotseat/D1`, `#garage`,\n`#replay/last`, `#about`, `#credits`, `#attract`, `#lab/blocks`, `#lab/physics`, `#menu/<page>`.\n\nLayout: `engine/` (the engine, its docs and tools; `engine/CHANGES.md` lists what was changed), `hub/session.js` (AI Hub\nclient, verbatim), `src/` (the game: `track/` blocks, mesher, physics, scenery; `car/` simulation, drawing, cameras;\n`race/` runs, ghosts, the bot, medals; `modes/`, `scenes/`, `editor/`, `ui/`, `audio/`, `story/`, `data/`), `tools/`\n(build, tests, bake, browser and hub checks). New content: add a turtle program to `src/data/tracks.js` (or export one\nfrom the editor's Dev Mode), then `node tools/bake.mjs`.\nEOF\necho ok","description":"Write the dev folder README"}}}
